wer/value "7{x}^{3}\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249295} {:answer/id #uuid "dd4b608f-ffe9-5210-b69f-f21778e1a218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-7\\text{ arctan }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249386}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248210} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b1cbd54-3439-59c4-a3d8-a241f241223c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "eb0e1654-81f3-51ff-a1ad-22ecef08f60d" :question/math-academy-id "q-114164" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (3{x}^{2}+\\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{arcsec}\\,x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}+\\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)+7(\\text{ arcsec }x)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+7\\text{ arcsec }x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250212 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0711b305-476f-5e9b-95eb-4506b57b1253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247489} {:answer/id #uuid "309f3a81-c1d7-5f83-83a5-b33a8ff29c95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247866} {:answer/id #uuid "50b82a9a-7db9-5132-9c63-46a9bdd51c58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248147} {:answer/id #uuid "6e49cf64-06ed-5c18-91c1-8b18124e4ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248402} {:answer/id #uuid "a2c445c7-0f68-5a44-9f25-9826793210bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248878}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248147} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bc5b4b1-ccde-5961-9955-b919105e6c58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9948b488-cf7d-5e1c-b375-ca22aa59712f" :question/math-academy-id "q-114252" :question/problem "$\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x{e}^{-x}-x+2{x}^{2}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=$" :question/worked-solution "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x{e}^{-x}-x+2{x}^{2}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[x{e}^{-x}-x+2{x}^{2}]^{′}}{[{sin}^{2}⁡x]^{′}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(1-x){e}^{-x}-1+4x}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(1-x){e}^{-x}-1+4x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x{e}^{-x}-x+2{x}^{2}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(1-x){e}^{-x}-1+4x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[(1-x){e}^{-x}-1+4x]^{′}}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x]^{′}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(x-2){e}^{-x}+4}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0-2){e}^{0}+4}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2+4}{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0251f12b-0bcd-5543-9eb5-f4ec7e4c9752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247439} {:answer/id #uuid "7229d8df-ae59-5660-b41e-cae11851e04c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248420} {:answer/id #uuid "91224b99-89c4-59ce-b789-19a10d61178d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{sec}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248714} {:answer/id #uuid "dc01fc34-a583-577b-8fdc-401ef22073b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3{csc}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249369} {:answer/id #uuid "f20a32cf-99d1-5344-b1f0-7a8da3242cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{csc}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249548}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247439} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec890aa8-f649-5040-b0db-08c864882cda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "de415510-24b2-53a0-b8c3-ddc9cdee62b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-114294" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identities $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$ and $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {\\left(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\right)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{4}}\\,(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{u}^{3}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{cos}^{3}⁡x}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250237 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e07b070-117b-50c5-9563-364f2b472707" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247691} {:answer/id #uuid "55dba241-a0ad-5dd2-a193-a8f4b6a32a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248201} {:answer/id #uuid "73e6af66-30b4-53c1-9d1f-0d00e757eaa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248442} {:answer/id #uuid "80fe39bd-6730-5d90-8ec2-9b32e504d4a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248563} {:answer/id #uuid "fc349b75-7a3e-573b-affc-74cf566b5683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249622}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248201} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0fb41b9-ef63-543e-b53e-dffe53d28fbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ea7a186f-be1a-52b9-b47f-3320d955e3e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114314" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{csc}^{2}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ where $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47c3019c-5b9e-5399-b786-04437705e092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248061} {:answer/id #uuid "6f81ffd7-1892-5f9b-9320-925504438589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248407} {:answer/id #uuid "89d313a8-f000-577f-a816-a34a6622496f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248650} {:answer/id #uuid "a7092c76-1bc1-50c0-b6c7-d05f207eda48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248909} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f08285-93fd-5b63-ade9-e4f908688cd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249429}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248061} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a1b567b-6514-5d16-ba8c-83023f80f2da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "062977fc-037b-5a67-9a07-c0d038a63f3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114318" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ and $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\n$$ to express this as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)] \\\\  & =-[1-\\sqrt{2}] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53a5ce15-8545-5507-9875-4858166892ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248177} {:answer/id #uuid "6e89cbc9-5e23-5e0b-b9bf-f6d1932ca856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248404} {:answer/id #uuid "89ea9e1a-7382-5ca5-a09c-8ea7c839b012" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248651} {:answer/id #uuid "de32f839-bded-50ef-83aa-fd6cbcc36cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249394} {:answer/id #uuid "f157fb56-50a8-596b-b6d5-8d047e671068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249541}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186249541} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0e45400-7471-5bcc-aded-c65faddf5ecc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2171a240-7846-596a-ba37-d0a6bdd37eb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114350" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡x=1-{cos}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({csc}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250252 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36808831-5f12-590d-b1a1-a51556ce1388" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247916} {:answer/id #uuid "5620cc5b-ac16-59b7-b164-a020fb71807f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248206} {:answer/id #uuid "62bf580f-e0bb-571e-9711-6c9ef20db080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248315} {:answer/id #uuid "989a05e7-89ad-5413-9c68-fe60f1d9157e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248786} {:answer/id #uuid "f59e1453-40ba-527d-9041-6931ffc32943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249567}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248315} :answer-field/id #uuid "45b59d92-a662-5e95-8231-080af1aa9b63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5c6112a4-1f7e-5aa3-8161-0a98a140a5f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-114353" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{4}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{4}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot 1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250264 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26e3b0c7-6ba8-5400-8ac8-7b37887b724a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247768} {:answer/id #uuid "2ef1714a-3e2f-5283-960d-0612d9cd18d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247846} {:answer/id #uuid "55a83628-ebd6-521c-b759-923519796757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248197} {:answer/id #uuid "92427487-b6ab-57d1-9010-4bf194bad822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248721} {:answer/id #uuid "a304e833-59e3-533b-ad04-51f239781600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248882}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247768} :answer-field/id #uuid "e92a6e21-0a01-536d-8e24-2a08a8cfe040" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "78ecd097-3d73-59be-9c42-4cecf987949e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114423" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250265 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029577c8-4387-5dce-abc1-e362769c0f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247442} {:answer/id #uuid "4e18de69-f618-587b-a2ec-5220370f7b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248124} {:answer/id #uuid "8d733b4b-1dca-53a4-a8f8-a44dd6bcbc93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248683} {:answer/id #uuid "a03c6caa-d5e0-51d2-ab76-a5150a905444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248854} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf847c0-a882-5640-8efa-f13f377ac775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249238}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248854} :answer-field/id #uuid "e155ce82-9147-55f3-82af-e32fec80f54d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "590fb4d1-46ef-5eb8-ba9c-0c9e6a8189ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-114429" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{sec}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{sec}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)] \\\\  & =-[2-\\sqrt{2}] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250266 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ba2385b-5f1b-5244-83c1-b965a5b9ded8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247525} {:answer/id #uuid "a5fb6d50-8041-58e2-9f41-ffe56c4a155d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248904} {:answer/id #uuid "b2498404-3d8c-5b85-8ac6-074b6583f6f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249021} {:answer/id #uuid "c54e170a-1b54-506c-a4cb-a0283c751651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249178} {:answer/id #uuid "d71dbf1d-cc4e-51d5-bf05-70348d2f6da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249326}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248904} :answer-field/id #uuid "5248ab5e-7d44-531f-99b3-9b3a257a9ca0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e264cd7f-f120-56f7-87e8-c3568e011399" :question/math-academy-id "q-114430" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (1+2x+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1+2x+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+{tan}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250267 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0342e2bb-429d-5c4b-bdcf-af0c133bed41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247447} {:answer/id #uuid "4da74220-54d0-547f-83a1-d55b8df0a746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248119} {:answer/id #uuid "781770b3-1cdc-564b-b5ae-c1b0aa778f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248479} {:answer/id #uuid "7dcc37dd-98c3-5f54-af8f-aa6f256316a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248527} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf390a3-5eae-5936-9074-6741445ddfeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249636}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186249636} :answer-field/id #uuid "28af24e1-dfb2-5a66-82cb-61a184f8439a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249749}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "26865ace-62b5-521c-a5d8-413469434ebb" :question/math-academy-id "q-114431" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{({tan}^{2}⁡x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250268 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03b7b03d-566b-57ff-9b57-89245c891150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247450} {:answer/id #uuid "258d518c-1393-51c3-9f47-dac610e236f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247755} {:answer/id #uuid "6da8f4fb-e78a-5608-aaf9-5f82ea791cb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248397} {:answer/id #uuid "6e400284-d57a-58fe-928b-40d3a6d7f47d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248400} {:answer/id #uuid "772c83ac-213f-55d7-9be6-27ef7871587f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248473}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248473} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e185e9d-354f-5cb8-8cd3-194e9a76c8b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "47d60902-14e4-57db-9a3c-83c4f5318199" :question/math-academy-id "q-114435" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =0-0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250269 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a05c2fc-f94d-5489-955e-6e93003cb216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4(\\pi -2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247662} {:answer/id #uuid "a3dc3121-d85d-555d-95fa-e1f130a553c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248887} {:answer/id #uuid "a75bb911-b1a2-59de-ac5b-2d5b63e7d0b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248911} {:answer/id #uuid "c53da061-88b8-5d38-9620-69fbe5f388d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249176} {:answer/id #uuid "e1bfdf52-8608-5e41-81ac-9c0e93199b37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249423}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248911} :answer-field/id #uuid "a980c72c-15a0-5296-ad73-7e85baf7f354" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3841fdbd-8341-5e24-9f59-0d6b99ab3106" :question/math-academy-id "q-114441" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-x){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\frac{\\pi }{4}] \\\\  & =[-0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[-1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+1+\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250270 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c892137-db18-57ab-a0c4-ee121e607cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247538} {:answer/id #uuid "4c2a7067-db8e-5098-bfe6-d1f90479e95e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2+\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248104} {:answer/id #uuid "6d0a2abd-f164-5bc3-8dd3-b337d3b3b315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248389} {:answer/id #uuid "ad009786-2f7e-5893-ae43-3dd8c76182ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248969} {:answer/id #uuid "f843f5bd-ea3e-5dce-a8a3-d0d60b0e0281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249589}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247538} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f0563b6-4107-5961-bf6f-8fdb92fa27b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5ae308dc-8f77-58de-a2c1-ae20d02ecf13" :question/math-academy-id "q-114454" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2+3{x}^{2}+2{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2+3{x}^{2}+2{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2{csc}^{2}⁡x+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{x}^{3}){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+{\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)}^{3}-[-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)+{\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)}^{3}] \\\\  & =-0+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{8}+2(1)-\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{64} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250271 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c4e702e-9e65-5bfb-8a82-fdb2e6001009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248105} {:answer/id #uuid "73736be6-741e-5fcb-9832-64df98a54b0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248435} {:answer/id #uuid "7c14fe49-14b9-5bf3-9972-457a5f71773c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{csc}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248515} {:answer/id #uuid "a0124f95-d6d1-5e40-a93d-70118a1d48a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{sec}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248851} {:answer/id #uuid "fbbf0464-a2cc-5e6f-b3e6-6072187e7744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249616}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186249616} :answer-field/id #uuid "3db888f0-dcaf-55b2-a986-3a13d12ea097" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "838376fb-3080-54c1-8fed-02688e1a872e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114457" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{{cot}^{5}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cot}^{5}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int -\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3558fbac-1b59-57fe-9bd0-f677f28f907a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247904} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbae598-1c6b-5eca-9ed6-66dceae7fb97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248275} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8c8c5c-01b7-553f-b6a2-1e3b22313e7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248700} {:answer/id #uuid "d23ea027-eba2-500a-9470-4d37e94b1732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249290} {:answer/id #uuid "d8f3cf69-d025-571c-b710-5dfbc6ea9479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249338}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248275} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9fe6922-c9ab-5e3a-bc26-b2f81f8df27d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8dcffc55-70b6-5a56-9948-97e923b1fff7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114460" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sin}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sin}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{3}⁡x(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{3}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250273 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01fdb005-8179-54c2-a098-7a92883a30b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247436} {:answer/id #uuid "339edf8e-b1b5-5c42-85d5-0ea922cac214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247890} {:answer/id #uuid "628f63d4-ac2f-5bae-a486-68847a2a7cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{cot}^{2}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248314} {:answer/id #uuid "a3803a20-435b-5eef-bd00-4200e4e0c33d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{tan}^{2}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248886} {:answer/id #uuid "c27eb4c6-5c1c-5c79-82eb-47c0d4c1cb3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249153}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247436} :answer-field/id #uuid "b025cb0b-872f-5b78-9d55-94c0d0e6743d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249980}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "35e08417-e875-5f7f-a591-7aa6eac3199b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114467" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{4}⁡(3x+2)+{cos}^{2}⁡(3x+2){sin}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ with $\\theta =3x+2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(3x+2)+{sin}^{2}⁡(3x+2)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{4}⁡(3x+2)+{cos}^{2}⁡(3x+2){sin}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x &= \\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡(3x+2)({cos}^{2}⁡(3x+2)+{sin}^{2}⁡(3x+2))}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &= \\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &= \\int {sec}^{2}⁡(3x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x+2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250274 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "429c4e06-3048-55b1-b208-72019f1b0474" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248017} {:answer/id #uuid "7e54eb59-7b2b-5295-a85f-69bab12eefd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248535} {:answer/id #uuid "8021e056-c15c-5db2-b077-c41b6d899f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248549} {:answer/id #uuid "848e9fc1-831c-51f0-9f79-1b100b19ee3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248600} {:answer/id #uuid "b94c2031-9662-5675-9f0a-6203b77aab15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249079}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248535} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0cd4974-971c-56d8-b46a-a70cd95372ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a520c33d-1aa5-5864-8fa9-daf66894b11e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114469" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ with $\\theta =2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})={sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x &= \\int \\frac{1}{[{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+1]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &= \\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &= \\int \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &= \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\text{d}x \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250275 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17074cab-3459-5914-a6fd-ff9fa965d1d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247633} {:answer/id #uuid "81a424ea-895b-5655-9e86-96e2b6d006e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-8\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248572} {:answer/id #uuid "ada25af1-a6cd-5ea9-ab11-56079d625a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248975} {:answer/id #uuid "d2346634-424b-580d-9fbc-d631630a3878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249288} {:answer/id #uuid "efe3a784-7995-56b3-978c-788102cf3100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249529}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186249288} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a18d560-640b-5d6d-8616-e9dd57c2577a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7da788f3-581f-57f3-a61d-5c56509defca" :question/math-academy-id "q-114473" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (8+8{cot}^{2}⁡(4x+3))\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ with $\\theta =4x+3,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡(4x+3)={csc}^{2}⁡(4x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (8+8{cot}^{2}⁡(4x+3))\\text{d}x & =8\\int (1+{cot}^{2}⁡(4x+3))\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\int {csc}^{2}⁡(4x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8[-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x+3)]+C \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x+3)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250277 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "294ec01d-16ec-5129-a5ad-20b579ee06d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247791} {:answer/id #uuid "3d365e84-3849-54a8-821f-4d24a73fbc3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(5x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247964} {:answer/id #uuid "7f136ce4-b6e2-5f01-bd33-5da390a739d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248541} {:answer/id #uuid "aec045a7-c97c-5a7e-8592-b75ce23f306a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248987} {:answer/id #uuid "e868382a-54c8-5c28-8250-a33c21643162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sec}⁡(5x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249475}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248987} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e84622e-de5e-5b8b-968b-5b509078c80e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8ce9a833-7138-5c70-a343-cfc3b184c5d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114510" :question/problem "Determine $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}⁡(5x-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ with $\\theta =5x-2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡(5x-2)={csc}^{2}⁡(5x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}⁡(5x-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x &= \\int \\frac{1}{[{cot}^{2}⁡(5x-2)+1]\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &= \\int \\frac{1}{{csc}^{2}⁡(5x-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &= \\int \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡(5x-2)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &= \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-2)\\text{d}x \\\\ &= -\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x-2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51767ce2-04dc-5c92-be64-ecdd456e4d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248156} {:answer/id #uuid "5af05724-0a68-584c-bdcc-e0f997546e41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248248} {:answer/id #uuid "a32c58bd-145a-53ec-98dc-145783470c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248884} {:answer/id #uuid "b0502d42-a25a-5ae1-9cca-dcf3a4cbe860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249008} {:answer/id #uuid "c64da03c-c464-59cb-81c9-d62f5d957afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249187}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186249008} :answer-field/id #uuid "a22fa253-1174-584a-9758-f3f964e75c1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "91292256-4f82-5669-95d9-e91e8b8d6af8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114552" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 2x{log}_{5}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{5}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5} \\\\ {v}^{′}=2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x{log}_{5}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡(x)({x}^{2})-\\int ({x}^{2})\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{log}_{5}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{log}_{5}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{5}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250283 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aec5f05-d22a-5c56-9672-60bc96c1bb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247519} {:answer/id #uuid "1f5abc59-c7e4-5c8a-87f4-b54b803742a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247702} {:answer/id #uuid "35fbcfa4-611f-5481-a5a0-e26daf32fe8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247912} {:answer/id #uuid "3e70e2aa-5270-59bd-8d76-329cce6e0fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247976} {:answer/id #uuid "e913e7e7-7377-58f1-a576-f2631769debf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249484}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247976} :answer-field/id #uuid "258426ca-e1eb-5f21-b193-8a88f0107073" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0ce30fbb-1b42-559b-a553-f2eb05e4f3a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-114553" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f7ca2da-40f3-525c-bac6-b29d8480b2e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247986} {:answer/id #uuid "a01808c9-616c-59db-89e8-974a2c400333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248852} {:answer/id #uuid "a30f743d-6b32-58c9-9c9b-527c9b8b888a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248883} {:answer/id #uuid "d8eb64cc-1ef2-5428-8c6b-e34b4c97b8be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249336} {:answer/id #uuid "f65d4aa5-8ff1-5c46-aa50-cef0172e5477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249573}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248852} :answer-field/id #uuid "80448976-ae2f-5f8d-b8a1-8ddcc578dda8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "67ee7e99-c327-5643-bad9-04c09862c4b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114556" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡(2x)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\left(-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}\\right)+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{4}⁡(2x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250288 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32c442b7-5812-5b9f-b5a3-9735de7bc5cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247886} {:answer/id #uuid "a66e4f08-82a7-51c7-9f0f-a316a7a82095" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-x}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248906} {:answer/id #uuid "aa1079b7-6c59-5146-a689-43939b214e55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248935} {:answer/id #uuid "c95f1123-d58f-569d-9f99-fc047c8ff23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+3x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249216} {:answer/id #uuid "fd5f9c6f-c38f-5d5f-aa01-a433d15de579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249639}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247886} :answer-field/id #uuid "260a912a-e53c-57b3-a2f5-20d936d8b8f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "805d5bf3-56e5-56a7-8a77-c98eb5fe1df0" :question/math-academy-id "q-114585" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{2}{2x+1} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\frac{2x}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use a substitution $2x+1=u,$ thus $2x=u-1$ and $\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\left(\\frac{2x}{2x+1}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\frac{u-1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\,\\text{d}u+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{u}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{u}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡u}{2}+D] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{2x+1}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{2}+D] \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=D-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}$ is an integral constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16bd605d-4c29-506c-8ce7-c84c48b67fc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247627} {:answer/id #uuid "34bd43f9-d4db-533f-acd2-5f7163057588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247897} {:answer/id #uuid "481e05e7-b62d-5851-a787-6a5d10613a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248068} {:answer/id #uuid "8e50b12e-9d6e-5a6e-8673-a420a275d68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248690} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5b9509-017e-5608-ad72-0fc4c95ad848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249611}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248068} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2a0c2c0-21f1-56dd-ac06-3f6bd57cc988" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "91699790-f225-57ae-8ea8-89f90b88a5ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-114679" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[uv{|}_{1/2}^{1}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x){|}_{1/2}^{1}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}x\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot 1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})-{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-x{|}_{1/2}^{1}\\,] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-0-(1-\\frac{1}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2132f021-21a8-5a4e-af38-2e7201ea6aa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247718} {:answer/id #uuid "35b40ac4-e4c4-5a30-8877-24568a7820dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247910} {:answer/id #uuid "372e873d-cdee-52c0-a20f-7c350588b44b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247922} {:answer/id #uuid "86138e57-324c-5532-8800-362d936df9ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248620} {:answer/id #uuid "cf400ea6-3cf8-51e3-b37b-9da66310f2fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249263}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247718} :answer-field/id #uuid "a610120c-3a38-5275-b0b0-50a70ca22c12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249961}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "005ce8c5-ca00-5c75-b19b-e74315abd5f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-114685" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (3{x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250299 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097b4ad7-3b82-591b-a4ad-f870dfcd7206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247507} {:answer/id #uuid "1569d1d0-fbb1-5b93-b963-9c9d29658e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247616} {:answer/id #uuid "2ab3bd00-0422-5967-9608-7bf73f86afe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247804} {:answer/id #uuid "55c81180-3fb7-5c0c-88dd-7f4bfb176ed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248200} {:answer/id #uuid "f19325bb-42d6-5612-a285-052a07fc365f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249546}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247616} :answer-field/id #uuid "031a055b-9447-51bf-8878-81d84171a278" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a74426e1-c72a-5f3f-acc7-d171cc86f36f" :question/math-academy-id "q-114687" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int (4-{cos}^{2}⁡4x+{sin}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x={cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4-{cos}^{2}⁡4x+{sin}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (4-[{cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x])\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4-\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250300 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c153176-f1be-574a-b61f-f35b724e9466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247532} {:answer/id #uuid "1130fb9f-a5c8-5014-9eac-4952653e89b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247577} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7f6fe8-e41a-559e-b3f5-c1a3707c68d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248395} {:answer/id #uuid "7d64c715-ce63-56cf-b8e4-f014fcf35e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248524} {:answer/id #uuid "9e55b908-564e-5263-ba81-3a007361a635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248829}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248395} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2d206e5-c570-5346-9baa-8117910d203b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6789bdc9-30dd-5df6-91b5-90b18efe1bb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114688" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({sin}^{2}⁡4x-{cos}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x={cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({sin}^{2}⁡4x-{cos}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250301 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "049104f3-f0f9-54a7-b34b-435d0972bf29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247457} {:answer/id #uuid "a4eaf12f-fe73-5186-a4a3-9f8f03675c77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248897} {:answer/id #uuid "a8ff8b54-32a2-5896-b5ee-9f76878d8456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248926} {:answer/id #uuid "bdae4aa9-7adc-544f-8974-b9d6969f616e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249110} {:answer/id #uuid "beaa505f-9480-5438-ad07-7fb3d61dda35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186249118} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9060f05-b9b2-57a4-af25-27550214ecdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "87059ed3-91f0-5463-8df6-00c144965662" :question/math-academy-id "q-114691" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 4{cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =2x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡2x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250304 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f4a15a-5034-5e4e-a608-b3f646db186e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{3x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247511} {:answer/id #uuid "16c0d414-1f11-53d0-852d-fc7267102858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247628} {:answer/id #uuid "62455da9-48ef-550d-a440-01a2ee5979f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248309} {:answer/id #uuid "853821a9-0766-5644-bceb-497ae5f69fc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248610} {:answer/id #uuid "c7a57500-2707-5bb0-be03-9a6fe0084671" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249198}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247511} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aeb11c3-2186-54f3-989f-bc6bf929857f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c6cefcd4-0ca3-54cc-a93f-201d1a8af19f" :question/math-academy-id "q-114696" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 4{cos}^{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\theta =x$ and substituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{cos}^{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {(2{cos}^{2}⁡x)}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the same formula $2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1$ with $\\theta =2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\frac{3}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+\\frac{3}{2}\\,x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{3x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250305 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "189f9213-0590-5763-b7f1-5a9ff40545ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247646} {:answer/id #uuid "303bff0b-8c8d-570e-932f-08f4f7631376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247859} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec7d7a9-63ea-5dcf-a82f-7b1c3d305145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248132} {:answer/id #uuid "5779c8af-d348-5133-a80a-b74659af00bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248217} {:answer/id #uuid "df03a416-02ac-502d-9685-963bd71eb91a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249403}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248217} :answer-field/id #uuid "a867ef71-90c3-5a94-8b9a-8d5a238e8997" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249966}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4cfdf230-d427-5945-b883-cca5a7c6a112" :question/math-academy-id "q-114698" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int {cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250307 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79350746-f178-547e-ba32-a73629e0bdee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248487} {:answer/id #uuid "80fdd38c-10cb-5e31-9bdf-05a2c0ede7d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248562} {:answer/id #uuid "a59d4ba7-54bc-5e85-8f04-df9ccb943007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248902} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0a71fe-aa09-5164-a615-0169aaa1adc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249239} {:answer/id #uuid "faefdfc4-dfa5-5604-b2ff-09b6d5b22666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249605}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248902} :answer-field/id #uuid "100ab088-a79d-58b2-9f15-678f690ca31e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7bceb2aa-4302-5440-9a58-9fffc3e95c17" :question/math-academy-id "q-114703" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int ({sin}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)={sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({sin}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d1e6aba-be6e-5ad9-a570-9f5b6c5579a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}-4x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247542} {:answer/id #uuid "24a1ac18-1b92-561d-9f2f-5b8340427947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247747} {:answer/id #uuid "60c4dea3-3499-52e9-be7b-e62e150e5240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}+x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248302} {:answer/id #uuid "80c59204-a318-55d0-882f-4c0026b93bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}-2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248557} {:answer/id #uuid "de29d0d8-e2ee-58e7-b612-b8e345c7aaf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249393}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186249393} :answer-field/id #uuid "95575fc0-fd7c-5a07-bb21-caf4767c4581" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "18d4b96f-8021-5acc-99b3-397a7e245847" :question/math-academy-id "q-114706" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (4{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (2\\cdot 2{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x-2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+6(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})+C \\\\  & =2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3{x}^{2}+C \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56b4881f-232b-5196-af35-aea7cb58e62b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248212} {:answer/id #uuid "5968f717-2e1f-500b-b4d7-ccdd473f65be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248233} {:answer/id #uuid "60480242-e3f6-5bd4-97c9-e03d8a634da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248296} {:answer/id #uuid "75629651-ad7e-5b79-a799-0589d593b3ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248455} {:answer/id #uuid "dfa029d1-b400-582d-911d-327f96487132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249406}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248296} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b0fcafe-3643-59b7-8506-b7d096e4d110" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249754}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "638cdd8d-a193-51d5-8d07-1c091b8aea29" :question/math-academy-id "q-114709" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int [1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250310 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c8e6af2-4d5c-5c2a-a223-b1581d70cf90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247539} {:answer/id #uuid "81d0e0bb-c0c1-5d45-a394-2bbf8970a683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248575} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8ed56a-5c7f-5ef2-81bb-dd4b2068da0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248685} {:answer/id #uuid "b663df30-c9cb-50e7-be06-34aabcf17e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249056} {:answer/id #uuid "ec862b5c-e91d-5ccc-9ab8-a560591305a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249501}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186249501} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3fd4bc8-95db-5454-a58a-0b3490f1540b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f620a8f2-ded3-5ab5-a180-a9e0b77ecbff" :question/math-academy-id "q-114712" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)]\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f54fcd2-11eb-5de2-b3f7-146de7b6348a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}+2{log}_{4}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247564} {:answer/id #uuid "407f3c19-f6db-5e87-b664-92774974ae3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x({log}_{4}⁡(x)+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247993} {:answer/id #uuid "8f0cac64-7a75-5a03-b08a-cee4bcbfa551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x({({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}+\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248695} {:answer/id #uuid "d24d95fe-f787-520e-9b19-d413da18936f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x({log}_{4}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249291} {:answer/id #uuid "e86cde0d-e490-5e48-8a63-d7e0865c34b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x({({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249477}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186249477} :answer-field/id #uuid "e420d51c-8836-5780-9cc3-1975930de065" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "40de2008-379c-588d-bf38-59107f150b43" :question/math-academy-id "q-114880" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int ({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}(x)-\\int (x)\\left(\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int {log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $$\n\\displaystyle \\int {log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{4}⁡(x))(x)-\\int (x)\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{4}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{4}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(x{log}_{4}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+D) \\\\  & =x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2x{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{2x}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\  & =x({({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡4})+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250314 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0566e525-d41b-5762-abad-a35a60fcea73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9e+12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247468} {:answer/id #uuid "377a31ef-b562-5a6f-805e-2834d145cfda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247923} {:answer/id #uuid "928f1290-d85e-54cd-bd20-3cfebd037b5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248724} {:answer/id #uuid "db06656d-5fcf-5439-bdb0-133473765928" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249358} {:answer/id #uuid "f4ff3e4b-d499-52d7-802f-f1d97113fff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9e-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249564}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186249564} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddcf16bb-2de3-57be-904f-fe6f88d0b63a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "25b1fd19-3728-5b2c-98ff-e3d6d85297ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-114883" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{e}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3}))(x)-\\int (x)\\left(\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x.\n$$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}))(x)-\\int (x)\\left(\\frac{3}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+D) \\\\  & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+18x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-6D.$ \n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+18x]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =[e{ln}^{2}⁡({e}^{3})-6e\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})+18e]-[(1){ln}^{2}⁡({1}^{3})-6(1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})+18(1)] \\\\  & =9e-18e+18e-18 \\\\  & =9e-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250319 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "082f5ffa-db8f-5b86-9f1f-66bec8888277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247495} {:answer/id #uuid "312a7284-86a2-58d1-925a-aae469b9cc31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}+2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247869} {:answer/id #uuid "4646f294-569b-5c9a-8e3f-8b4bffc32dd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1-2e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248052} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1ab61f-f876-54ff-ac9a-719572398e93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248654} {:answer/id #uuid "aed8ce21-2fef-51ea-932a-bf3d76234eac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248988}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248654} :answer-field/id #uuid "90297971-15bc-5633-a065-ce4100255f03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "dca36867-5a6f-51bd-9e64-ad043dde12a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-114900" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{e}4x({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4x({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}(2{x}^{2})-\\int (2{x}^{2})\\left(\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int x{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\text{d}x.\n$$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{3}⁡x)\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4x({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{x}^{2}({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}{ln}^{2}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{4D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$ \n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}4x({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡e-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+1)-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2-2+1)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(0-0+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250322 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31c17a05-d2f9-5ba0-b754-dcbfc7f9b4eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}\\left(\\frac{x-3}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247879} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccaaf30-f65e-532d-85cd-8c1ce995b1fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248111} {:answer/id #uuid "8f1dda95-180f-5a89-bfe9-5307962c3d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248697} {:answer/id #uuid "c56c203a-3635-5203-8a26-4d2596b69db1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249180} {:answer/id #uuid "ec86287a-069c-51b9-9eb7-959c7a23a3fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(2(x-3))+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249500}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248697} :answer-field/id #uuid "83644fa9-f278-5c29-b9fd-b62b8c892acc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d48157cd-3ea4-5a4b-b2a2-ea19ff6fa51b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114923" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{2}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-3).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x-3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x-3|\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(u)+C \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-3)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250323 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29dcd689-72bf-5686-8310-3f4ea4bcf96f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\text{arcsec}(2x-7)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247794} {:answer/id #uuid "7314371c-12e4-5b55-aa71-8b0815acf1f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(2x-7)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248430} {:answer/id #uuid "87412b14-93b3-5355-a1a5-6ed1ad4a5e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(2x-7)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248633} {:answer/id #uuid "a875d9a9-1360-585e-bc17-f8dabea475cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{arcsec}(2x-7)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248921} {:answer/id #uuid "cd50af5e-b746-5d70-8359-da9db445f575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\text{arcsec}(2x-7)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248430} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecf1fad6-0be7-535a-8535-84a302eff6c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d6c81b22-316a-514d-b9b9-16489eee9df0" :question/math-academy-id "q-114926" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{4}{|2x-7|\\sqrt{(2x-7)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4}{|2x-7|\\sqrt{(2x-7)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\frac{1}{|2x-7|\\sqrt{(2x-7)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(2x-7).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=2x-7.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4}{|2x-7|\\sqrt{(2x-7)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\frac{1}{|2x-7|\\sqrt{(2x-7)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(u)+C \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{arcsec}(2x-7)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250324 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "001d516e-ba06-5b95-b4a6-f35dab9a3672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}(x+4)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247415} {:answer/id #uuid "14ed51ee-756e-57ce-98c5-e09580d0ea4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247613} {:answer/id #uuid "1d6dbd24-53a8-57ca-8ab3-2c785beb7617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247686} {:answer/id #uuid "3fd72e51-75ac-59c4-906c-a14dfbeed5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}\\left(\\frac{x-4}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247990} {:answer/id #uuid "4deeee7d-3bfe-54f3-bb50-f18cec4519b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}\\left(\\frac{x+4}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248123}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247686} :answer-field/id #uuid "8347f822-40d4-57c9-9262-ff4fdf512681" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "07920739-bd19-5b4b-b343-8e19ac7c6d5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114928" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+15 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+15 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-8x+16)-16+15 \\\\  & =(x-4)^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{(x-4)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x-4.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{(x-4)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(x-4)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "069e5dc3-903f-56c3-80b2-a36d93cb6a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247483} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee8a822-9e03-5b0b-9157-4a6e261fd6ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{arcsec}(2(x+2))+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248134} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9b7170-e2cb-5afb-ae16-7aa25d17f2fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248268} {:answer/id #uuid "8c688811-e631-576f-b3af-fccf1d19453f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}\\left(\\frac{x+2}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248679} {:answer/id #uuid "c73082f2-4cbb-5c23-891d-47290806832d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{arcsec}\\left(\\frac{x-2}{2}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249194}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248268} :answer-field/id #uuid "76fa23d1-4298-5709-9837-39a75683bfac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fd2cd352-82c1-595a-88b3-99447daccebc" :question/math-academy-id "q-114929" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x+3 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+({2}^{2}-{2}^{2})+3 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+4x+4)-4+3 \\\\  & =(x+2)^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $x+2.$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution \n\n$$\nu=x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|x+2|\\sqrt{(x+2)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(x+2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250326 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01c50259-96ff-5091-b6d8-d010aabcd87a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{2}-3}{4{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247435} {:answer/id #uuid "5b1b58be-7936-591f-a3c9-e22825f21d58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248249} {:answer/id #uuid "602d95a8-3c49-5628-a5fc-26ae6d4442af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4{e}^{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248293} {:answer/id #uuid "ae45cdbd-b5db-5833-8170-fccfe8733b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248981} {:answer/id #uuid "f16fc0ad-7654-55ab-873b-8984cf712d78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249543}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248981} :answer-field/id #uuid "46bceeef-1e66-56f1-87c4-0b40ebcc4c53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c7237523-38ec-5167-93d0-30747905ffb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114942" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{e}9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=9{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=3{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}(3{x}^{3})-\\int (3{x}^{3})\\left(\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $$\n\\displaystyle \\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{2}⁡x)\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+D) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{3}{ln}^{2}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{3})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{6D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$\n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{3})]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡e-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+\\frac{2}{3})-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3-2+\\frac{2}{3})-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(0-0+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\frac{2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f84bc89-0f5f-5174-b311-6b1ac207d432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4e-8}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248845} {:answer/id #uuid "acd12eca-de9b-50f1-ae82-10635e26c184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e-6}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248968} {:answer/id #uuid "f04115a5-6b2e-5bc2-9ed5-4e7dbb828a37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249532} {:answer/id #uuid "f2594c73-abaa-58dd-995b-af12abd8461c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3{e}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249549} {:answer/id #uuid "f538ac92-7bb7-5776-a593-eda1db9ee897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4e+3}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249565}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248845} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b1851a2-09ca-5e98-9283-451c4f3c0948" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ee94ab2f-1f66-5795-8930-e1ab98c8dab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114944" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{e}{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\int (x)\\left(\\frac{4{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $$\n\\displaystyle \\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))(x)-\\int (x)\\left(\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D) \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{8x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+\\frac{8x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+8)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{4D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+8)]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({e}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})+8)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({1}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{2})+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(4-8+8)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(0-0+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{4e-8}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250330 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21fa41e6-4e3a-5806-859d-c2aaa4b58edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247725} {:answer/id #uuid "3aad9910-8581-517c-bee6-27e599bcdafd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247943} {:answer/id #uuid "81ff4d92-1a10-5646-988f-1c901a51022f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248576} {:answer/id #uuid "9f6e5a27-6ad8-5b1a-b327-7847f10b1222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248844} {:answer/id #uuid "cefcf51a-b70a-5c3a-a3be-b1a5d98e9adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249260}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248576} :answer-field/id #uuid "6117be46-83ef-580f-84ce-56c76fa2d084" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4f09819e-da12-5415-9b7c-4388f9ed375d" :question/math-academy-id "q-114952" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$ using integration by parts." :question/worked-solution "First, we let\n\n$$\nI=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{2}⁡x\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\right)\\left(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $I,$ remembering to add a constant of integration $C$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2I \\\\ 3I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{12}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "522547ac-6535-5fb0-b8a3-a2053a87b01d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248161} {:answer/id #uuid "5dffb7ca-1a66-52ae-b04f-97ae522f8f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248279} {:answer/id #uuid "751980ea-1704-5381-ae28-6aa05cfad2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248453} {:answer/id #uuid "90fe0781-abfd-56c8-9147-cf8bdbde8121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248713} {:answer/id #uuid "9d475fa0-a4da-59e4-b41c-47c13378b87f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248823}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248453} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0704fd5-1897-52d9-acd5-2f3d7565c6ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "85a3e0f2-59ad-5501-8562-0840b6094216" :question/math-academy-id "q-114965" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$ using integration by parts." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $$\n\\displaystyle I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{6}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{6{ln}^{5}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{6}⁡x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\left(\\frac{6{ln}^{5}⁡x}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{7}⁡x-6\\int \\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{7}⁡x-6I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={ln}^{7}⁡x-6I \\\\ 7I & ={ln}^{7}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{7}⁡x}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}({ln}^{7}⁡x){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}({ln}^{7}⁡(e)-{ln}^{7}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c0432af-5e36-5fda-8917-32b349683fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247816} {:answer/id #uuid "38592cbc-383b-5e42-b2c1-16c799f4dac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247927} {:answer/id #uuid "472b2169-b73e-52b2-a759-79ee2c0017dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248056} {:answer/id #uuid "a124094c-2198-56e3-a44a-8e218a714881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248864} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c76c8f-f2d8-5896-8bd2-98aa7de77cc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249157}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186249157} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfceba82-e7c8-58e8-a6e1-6dbed0dd06ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "aafbcc52-b05c-5248-b40a-c0ce083a128b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114999" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$ using integration by parts." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $$\n\\displaystyle I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{9}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{9{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{9}⁡x)\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\right)\\left(\\frac{9{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9I \\\\ 10I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{40}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{40}({ln}^{10}⁡x){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}({ln}^{10}⁡(e)-{ln}^{10}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a841c83-c0e9-5548-b814-ce0a3ffb2d21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461719} {:answer/id #uuid "2e47707c-e2a1-5139-bc7e-e581dc66eb9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461720}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461719} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc3e7cd3-ca1a-58c4-9300-8f544b1abaec" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /4}{sin}^{5}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462613} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b9b9bc7-befc-5680-8c8c-18aa54ebb0c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461721} {:answer/id #uuid "77cf71b4-bf47-50db-9251-b4e0e740d066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461722}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461722} :answer-field/id #uuid "e594767d-c8a4-5f3c-b4d7-646f2605402e" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{3}+{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462614} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eecadbbf-c020-5e7f-900a-560bd7259f38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461723} {:answer/id #uuid "a36b0bc7-28e6-5d80-978c-9eaa714d757f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461724}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461724} :answer-field/id #uuid "13ab1077-5e87-549f-9136-2d3a0ac9fbe4" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c52ca68f-33c1-5cf6-9bde-bf78ae92f92f" :question/math-academy-id "q-115275" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to $0$ due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)={sin}^{5}⁡x$ is an odd function, but integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /4}{sin}^{5}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\n$$ is not of the form $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$ since the upper and lower limits are not opposites. Therefore, we cannot use symmetry to simplify the integral.\n\n- The function $g(x)={x}^{3}+{x}^{5}$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =(-x)^{3}+(-x)^{5} \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}+(-{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-{x}^{5} \\\\  & =-({x}^{3}+{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =-g(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{3}+{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)={x}^{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-x) & =(-x)^{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(-x)) \\\\  & =-{x}^{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x) \\\\  & =-h(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{3}+{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x;\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e1be917-67fb-578e-954b-abd43a23e348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247974} {:answer/id #uuid "50cbb7df-ff1d-5ec1-b975-423eb45cf6ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248148} {:answer/id #uuid "5a30d855-606b-58c6-b70c-741050c6c8e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248240} {:answer/id #uuid "c1157ca6-9bce-51d1-a9ee-ceec63429c58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249140} {:answer/id #uuid "ce75318e-e092-5621-a3d1-bcdfb26a886b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249253}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248240} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e8ddb9e-3675-514c-a828-85dac3fe037b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ef69b6da-6b79-5e57-a05c-34b900661ea4" :question/math-academy-id "q-115517" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are $\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{1}{x}=\\infty $ and $\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x} & =\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{{[\\frac{1}{x}]}^{′}}{{[\\operatorname{cot}⁡x]}^{′}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\left(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\right)}{-{csc}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={(\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x} & ={(\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x})}^{2} \\\\  & ={(\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]^{′}}{[x]^{′}})}^{2} \\\\  & ={(\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1})}^{2} \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)}^{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250425 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d36f99a-7b3c-58c4-8e9a-3a21fd763566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247544} {:answer/id #uuid "61a4653f-6df7-51f2-86fa-d13ae68764a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248305} {:answer/id #uuid "8b2148f7-50e6-51e7-9398-cf6ddcd9de74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248668} {:answer/id #uuid "a11b1bc5-2153-59a0-816b-97eff84bc81f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248863} {:answer/id #uuid "db8f7095-8449-5145-9fef-5d8ca09214f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249361}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247544} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd93bb03-4956-5c3c-8d6a-9abd4a3f4f9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a4bbbb84-0fac-5f07-a8f5-38985b38226e" :question/math-academy-id "q-115518" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are $$\n\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-\\infty \n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)=\\infty ,\n$$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{-\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)} & =\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)]^{′}}{{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)]}^{′}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{\\left(-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\right)} \\\\  & =-\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\left(\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\right){cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =-{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250427 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1876b234-1e20-59a3-9257-ae9d5cc33aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247642} {:answer/id #uuid "247f2508-da04-5060-824a-40e6d3bc76ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247744} {:answer/id #uuid "5446abbd-737c-5a8c-8f28-a299c5842d91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248181} {:answer/id #uuid "5d2f84f2-f002-5bd8-9d6f-31d437aac8e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248271} {:answer/id #uuid "ffba6739-e919-55dc-a83a-e96b4762eeb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249663}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248271} :answer-field/id #uuid "3280d34f-e5de-5288-a6ba-c82c61ac0a77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8d5a6bfe-2213-5fca-8027-6b27cb0a5f81" :question/math-academy-id "q-115523" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are $\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\infty $ and $\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}} & =\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{[\\operatorname{tan}⁡x]^{′}}{{[{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}]}^{′}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡x}}{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to {\\frac{\\pi }{2}}^{-}}\\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250428 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b693811-a16b-53ed-9611-68583bdf136e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247672} {:answer/id #uuid "2d4b941c-69b2-577b-a723-cb390aecaad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247825} {:answer/id #uuid "52a8d6c1-c802-52b6-9422-b177b1c39eeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248165} {:answer/id #uuid "644a1b11-e2aa-55cd-ba47-d5a074cd81d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248329} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0fcf86-6e40-5292-948f-778a8f8317e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248531}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248329} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fb56519-add1-5a22-b89f-f23b73f9e1db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f0b7651b-eacd-5715-8331-dab57a1d4302" :question/math-academy-id "q-115526" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are $\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-\\infty $ and $\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{-\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x} & =\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)]}^{′}}{[\\operatorname{cot}⁡x]^{′}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\right)}{-{csc}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\right)} \\\\  & =-\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250430 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d037599-07ed-5ba7-83e9-f8c1efa482f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247821} {:answer/id #uuid "31ae4547-e21a-58af-ba30-0bdc4c6faf8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247874} {:answer/id #uuid "88431084-d59b-514f-a06a-1a663f1974b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248641} {:answer/id #uuid "d2dfa8ec-c233-56f4-9f06-28d24d2fad3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249296} {:answer/id #uuid "f67649d3-0d90-50b6-8568-82074b23672e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249574}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186249296} :answer-field/id #uuid "38f9bf5f-e290-5c3d-ab0c-661753693c04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e116ffff-24eb-5f64-952b-b5d8dd36f71b" :question/math-academy-id "q-115530" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are $\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\sqrt{x}=\\infty $ and $\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }{ln}^{2}⁡x=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} & =\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[\\sqrt{x}]^{′}}{{[{ln}^{2}⁡x]}^{′}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{x}{4\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} & =\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[\\sqrt{x}]^{′}}{[4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]^{′}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{4}{x}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{x}{8\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\lim_{x\\to \\infty }\\sqrt{x} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "010fae26-d218-5d85-80be-b5da7fa03138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{xln⁡4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250562} {:answer/id #uuid "053f36b4-6fc7-536b-8778-64782d3f6eec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{cot}^{4}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250595} {