orrect {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252504} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e5bd1bd-eab3-5250-8633-db4827abfabb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "605f5d22-0a36-54b2-9fda-393ada9a651b" :question/math-academy-id "q-11653" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle M=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & w \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(M)=2$, what is the value of $w?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & w \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-w\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4w.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nSince $det(M)=2$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =2 \\\\ 6-4w & =2 \\\\ -4w & =2-6 \\\\ -4w & =-4 \\\\ w & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253311 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3458a089-3888-542e-968d-c9518a04e88d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461815} {:answer/id #uuid "50778f05-ddf5-582c-8db9-cc7782d783f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461816}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461816} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eca055b-5464-5837-a901-254ea6c3a13c" :answer-field/key "$H=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0abc8f03-a6b8-5309-9492-8dc139b5f6cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461817} {:answer/id #uuid "9c816193-4544-54b9-b7d7-6c9d022fe5bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461818}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461818} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf477f3-ea09-51a1-9a9b-7b55b2cadfda" :answer-field/key "$J=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73ab26a4-2324-5b3c-8149-15706d53927d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461819} {:answer/id #uuid "f92a8eac-48f4-5940-81c5-cfc73dbdf656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461820}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461819} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d8dc630-97cd-5342-89aa-58a8996e2070" :answer-field/key "$K=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "87ca815d-8c8d-5ffa-9415-2a57d9bd87a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-11717" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $H$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(H)=5\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(H)=0,$ we conclude that $H$ is not invertible. Since $H$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $H$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $J$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(J)=2\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(J)=0,$ we conclude that $J$ is not invertible. Since $J$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $J$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $K$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\nTherefore, only $H$ and $J$ is singular."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097794a2-c7ca-5ecf-bd92-2d6b9637edf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250639} {:answer/id #uuid "87862fd4-0b9f-5398-911d-63cce6d1b136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251692} {:answer/id #uuid "c745fe31-0cba-5f79-a40c-985ece6242bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252314} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e5419b-2e45-5470-ad3f-325c6e4e71dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252419} {:answer/id #uuid "e279ed19-5a71-5d13-9f8d-6703bfc76869" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252544}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250639} :answer-field/id #uuid "886a0983-97da-5781-96e9-27635821fd09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "18e87006-2d52-52b3-8fdf-cef524aa5a2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-11719" :question/problem "If $F=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & t \\\\ t & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $F$ is singular if and only if $det(F)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =3\\cdot 3-t\\cdot t \\\\  & =9-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =9 \\\\ t & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $t$ are $t=\\pm 3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57d016cc-b32a-556a-872a-d9d9454755e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251269} {:answer/id #uuid "7f24ab14-2022-5d0d-aa61-084ff480fc31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251621} {:answer/id #uuid "ac0e0abc-a204-57f0-a0ca-d651601dc526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252047} {:answer/id #uuid "e207ec5b-404c-50f6-acae-784dfe8e282b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252541} {:answer/id #uuid "f8fa13d3-a4d7-5bb5-8a44-96e5e778acbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252733}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252047} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9e9e596-1625-5316-9294-354fbe58edae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e6398e19-0166-5ea2-9ff8-a93fab46629b" :question/math-academy-id "q-11721" :question/problem "If $Q=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ x & x\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $Q$ is singular if and only if $det(Q)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =3\\cdot x-x\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3x-6x \\\\  & =-3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $x$ is $x=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253320 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "783db2fd-7825-5c2a-a37c-ecf12e9a46b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251550} {:answer/id #uuid "78c0bab0-9b03-5269-8dab-8e7ea4106e4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251554} {:answer/id #uuid "8c394e4f-1154-5d85-9535-8a7a4b1a9b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251736} {:answer/id #uuid "9180c1c8-1f7c-540a-8d44-d585577c0e83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251795} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f59c7d-fd33-58d7-ae00-8babf85da183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252288}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251554} :answer-field/id #uuid "e38d674a-89c9-50fe-9a20-d74c11c871f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0c7b9ea7-cded-56a3-a2f3-1334f92c0300" :question/math-academy-id "q-11726" :question/problem "If $P=\\begin{bmatrix}n & -8 \\\\ -2 & n\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $n.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $P$ is singular if and only if $det(P)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =n\\cdot n-(-2)\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & ={n}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {n}^{2} & =16 \\\\ n & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $n$ are $n=\\pm 4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fede3ab-03ba-569b-bc73-b40000997af0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250823} {:answer/id #uuid "27da4a10-7106-529e-afc0-bd91fc3f3b49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3-4{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250894} {:answer/id #uuid "42f42797-7b5d-5144-b16e-6c1575823d99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251114} {:answer/id #uuid "7de54d6e-8542-5a9a-85c4-d974c2a7462d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251609} {:answer/id #uuid "80b26266-a183-516d-b9da-db708dac8ad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2+5e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251636}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251609} :answer-field/id #uuid "52011555-7d4c-59cd-aa5f-137a92984e86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c930269f-7d7b-579b-a107-b0f3bde563e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-117291" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ if $$\n\\displaystyle f(x)={\\int }_{x}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{x}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{x}^{a}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\nThe integrand ${e}^{1-{t}^{2}}$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying the FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-{x}^{2}}+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){e}^{1-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-{x}^{2}}-{e}^{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-{x}^{2}}-{e}^{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${f}^{′}(0).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-{e}^{1-{0}^{2}}-{e}^{{sin}^{2}⁡0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-0}-0 \\\\  & =-e.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253472 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86be746b-a100-5c81-b09c-64f69d52354d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡\\left(\\frac{7x}{4}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251684} {:answer/id #uuid "a9d165e4-04cb-5b98-939c-960f26cf5112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{4}-sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252020} {:answer/id #uuid "b0256387-7df1-50a5-82ff-d81ca490f07f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{7}{4}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252091} {:answer/id #uuid "b49f046c-976a-5805-b1b1-2b7abb41fb1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡x-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252141} {:answer/id #uuid "d4f0698c-7c2c-5b62-addb-c963a8f40249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡(x+\\frac{7}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252436}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252091} :answer-field/id #uuid "deb567f0-6e17-59cc-ad2c-c94c01211c94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8212d812-45a7-565f-b087-e2f78df1febe" :question/math-academy-id "q-118348" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f2d3945780d6d042ae5fa01905cf7740fca0f5f80307124556a1b4724f691683.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the graph shown above?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/6b/6ba976f250811d1ba3109f4aecbfdb2a4de4ee86300fa867e80e2087aa21601f.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-sin⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $\\frac{7}{4}$ to give $y=-\\frac{7}{4}sin⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-\\frac{7}{4}sin⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253474 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4755537d-9558-58e3-b1fb-e15adf27ad35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡(x-\\frac{1}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251146} {:answer/id #uuid "4f6bddc5-a5cd-5875-abbb-9f22efb60464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251203} {:answer/id #uuid "6b736f08-32b3-5af6-a82e-5816f1c230a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}-sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251431} {:answer/id #uuid "790ade44-b249-5c2c-8b0f-5e62399db5ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{4}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251558} {:answer/id #uuid "cdec9314-5fd3-5b0f-8a26-a6c75f8c9e96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡x-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252370}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251558} :answer-field/id #uuid "5268f851-1f31-5f10-a461-a1a9a49c25a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c5a416a1-a537-5d81-9140-46bc32e0a299" :question/math-academy-id "q-118350" :question/problem "![](images/a0/a065146d50b16eade39c758b59e13994272cf7180aaa662008a1865e4160421e.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the graph shown above?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/46/46e8f92e758c7f4643b64c05d0b457f7b99b6723ddf9be9cd63da28079b89618.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-sin⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, compress it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $\\frac{1}{4}$ to give $y=-\\frac{1}{4}sin⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{4}sin⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11887f2a-0a24-59b1-bf52-70443332e782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=0.5cos⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250704} {:answer/id #uuid "827718fa-59e7-5f42-a657-8daf1ad225ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-cos⁡x-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251653} {:answer/id #uuid "9a6ed2a9-c0b6-57c5-9f9b-e625d0bc47f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-cos⁡(0.5x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251879} {:answer/id #uuid "f27a34d6-db05-5604-9599-14b648b40515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-cos⁡(x-0.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252676} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb750cd-0800-57d9-8519-419d69437235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-0.5cos⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252800}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252800} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec5bfc21-496a-51a3-96e1-9cb079e7ba71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c17ec7a1-cf6a-525c-a5a6-62aa532c5d59" :question/math-academy-id "q-118352" :question/problem "![](images/92/92f4cd47e9046d9fcd37ac105d89c5a78c0c3635ab66c3a1a194e7d24e1f3f39.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the graph shown above?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/8c/8c4b58c0e0508fbea7df9619b8086fd70d1a367df36e31d0d7b9ecc7eb0f4378.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-cos⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, compress it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $0.5$ to give $y=-0.5cos⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-0.5cos⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253477 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f87115a-14a1-5420-b12f-4de7f649d669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250689} {:answer/id #uuid "146ecfce-1448-5a29-83ac-57f0c818f6f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)}{x-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250731} {:answer/id #uuid "4d2b7b12-3622-5c07-b56e-efc218ab6e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)}{2x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251192} {:answer/id #uuid "67e6f369-d372-5be3-90e5-cfbaea46d954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251406} {:answer/id #uuid "f4e573dd-a438-59c4-8aee-e4622e8a762f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252699}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250731} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e0ba76f-ec8d-5bcb-94c4-5096b03b298a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "aaabba1b-1cf6-581c-b6c1-fff29f9ff6a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-118387" :question/problem "![](images/3a/3ae609102d5545d3db2e035238f030e3ee1b58be8aba716224d5df967ca6ed5a.png)\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the point $P$ on the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)$ that is closest to the origin (as shown above) satisfies the equation \n\n$$\n2x+=0.\n$$\n\n \nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the *squared* distance $S$ between $(0,0)$ and a general point $P(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(x,y) & =(x-0)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe require that the point $P$ lies on the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2).$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2))^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+{ln}^{2}⁡(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the minimum distance, we take the first derivative of $S(x)$ and equate it to zero. This gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{′}(x)=2x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{x-2} & =0 \\\\ 2x+\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)}{x-2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253480 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31777cec-aa4a-531c-8f91-1af7a0f66a13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-cos⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250973} {:answer/id #uuid "3c737870-c937-5be1-9306-cc57cf97a411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251056} {:answer/id #uuid "4c303ce3-dff7-58a3-b70c-6bed684870f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-cos⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251183} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c0f728-a1b5-55fd-890b-dbd31577858c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=sin⁡(1-x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252145} {:answer/id #uuid "e3100428-23e3-5316-a71c-cc8576b92026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡(1-x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252551}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251056} :answer-field/id #uuid "011a22c2-f8f2-5ad2-9c5f-c7e5ef1ebd65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e1484f94-afd5-5ba7-9351-7b1e33dca84c" :question/math-academy-id "q-118450" :question/problem "![](images/98/98e3dc2a664f5096d2b7c9ba7bf7fc56faa189cd573a3de462e0b249fbc90af6.png)\n\nIdentify the equation that generated the graph above." :question/worked-solution "![](images/84/8499856915baa0bf144561dd35143e024586f4d417ac4f9c1ee48d7586e0f26c.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-sin⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, translate it by $1$ unit **down** to give $y=-sin⁡x-1.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-sin⁡x-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253481 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a82af2-7a13-5897-a4e5-be7ce6270303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250617} {:answer/id #uuid "3a8e986a-de9c-521d-b881-ca9496650e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=cos⁡(-x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251040} {:answer/id #uuid "76df98ee-93fe-538f-8008-c6ddf54fc9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-cos⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251533} {:answer/id #uuid "c189cf42-9038-5ed3-b121-e05c9f81c20c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252260} {:answer/id #uuid "c55c4bf8-5929-50f8-ad79-710124faf1d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-cos⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252300}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251533} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba48c244-1e49-5d29-9375-b61fd2f958e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bde136cf-b853-5290-a074-d60c0c0656c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-118454" :question/problem "![](images/d2/d2bda3c0e8f9d19c67074209a9f42617b5814dae505e7f917a5a6f89012b8a87.png)\n\nIdentify the equation that generated the graph above." :question/worked-solution "![](images/ac/ac75968867bedffb5ff090a0ca0ab3457e7107fb4b30be36899b79c3e16809b7.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-cos⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, translate it by $1$ unit **down** to give $y=-cos⁡x-1.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-cos⁡x-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253525 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ae3c5e0-1352-56fd-ba70-9a98aacdb051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250782} {:answer/id #uuid "3b8d8918-9739-590c-9fbc-5d363870224a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{2x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251048} {:answer/id #uuid "7590b4e3-175b-5973-b9a4-23a24a9d8b1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{2x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251521} {:answer/id #uuid "d65bc188-62c5-5f03-8494-a8fcd839865a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=2{e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252450} {:answer/id #uuid "dbcc7213-5543-5c22-a097-9b55ce7076ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252486}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252486} :answer-field/id #uuid "d173063d-47e4-520d-a7a8-338e552ab61b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a130453a-6065-5959-8de8-bb802e7d41f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-118885" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}{cos}^{2}⁡y$ for $0<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}{cos}^{2}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡y & ={e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253529 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "010fae26-d218-5d85-80be-b5da7fa03138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{xln⁡4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250562} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7274d3-9d6c-566f-8ab0-5d6dadc206db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250801} {:answer/id #uuid "3fea77d7-dd38-54a3-ab38-de4a5e6af670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{xln⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251082} {:answer/id #uuid "90d31982-431c-5c96-9fd1-28cbe6930c37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{xln⁡4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251788} {:answer/id #uuid "e56177c0-fb1c-54a8-8c75-934ef63a1c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252561}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251788} :answer-field/id #uuid "35ef16c9-7f8c-57e6-86fd-b4dbee5a6bfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b9de855f-8e10-5bff-89a6-c3649ce380b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-11900" :question/problem "Given that $y=5{log}_{4}⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{log}_{4}⁡x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}⁡x) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{xln⁡4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253538 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "061e9049-685a-5e57-b12d-6b56030be323" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250602} {:answer/id #uuid "42b59196-b9a8-573b-be83-9fd902357365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={2}^{x}{ln}^{2}⁡2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251109} {:answer/id #uuid "b5960315-6cae-5802-922d-5b341c99ee9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252150} {:answer/id #uuid "c18c981b-dd26-58f1-bd40-912972cd4a5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252261} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e95291-17f3-571b-b000-bb1e43ebce08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252574}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250602} :answer-field/id #uuid "e27e7bd7-eaed-55b0-916c-a3dd3a5a5d99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4f9dee74-c92e-5523-b157-7ba038c745c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119044" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-{2}^{x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{2}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{2}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\left(\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\right)+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253547 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26bf5cf8-eaf1-5b10-8d2a-662c31b3b508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250885} {:answer/id #uuid "783b0f4c-199c-5928-b08e-dcb4df838be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2+\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251549} {:answer/id #uuid "89f1e417-01f6-5b82-ba77-84fd142edcc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251714} {:answer/id #uuid "e0afa8a6-a60b-5d30-b8a6-b2c64b3b9e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x+\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252532} {:answer/id #uuid "fe2d11d8-637f-5d1f-abb2-68fd4be88574" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2+\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252782}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252782} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef06db64-440f-52c2-ab98-0824b44d15d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253222}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2a7a5557-d240-5298-a285-f0853a897b06" :question/math-academy-id "q-11911" :question/problem "Given that $y=2x+ln⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+ln⁡x) \\\\  & =2+\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cb5d83c-b113-5e49-8ad1-b7af79795399" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250661} {:answer/id #uuid "134a924c-2d79-5a81-a5e4-b32b5f6f1568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8ln⁡8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250720} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6aaf6a-f7c4-5c7f-bd3f-349e7ca5691e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{ln⁡8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251444} {:answer/id #uuid "de9d5bb2-c832-5736-b2a1-be6b5d245d22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252513} {:answer/id #uuid "e065e44d-7317-5a6d-9dae-1e8e400b8d8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252529}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252513} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a2d08ee-6e6a-5895-bb57-f6640a579319" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b9e0ca00-8b2a-5d3e-84fd-62f2c13cf2f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-11930" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=ln⁡(8x)$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here $f(x)=ln⁡(8x)$ is a function of a function. We use the chain rule.First, we express $g(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=8x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8x}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{8x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{8}}{\\cancel{8}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253567 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d7b3388-0623-533e-bfdf-9f2c6f502040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2xln⁡{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250941} {:answer/id #uuid "416392e1-706e-5bf2-9d81-60e36e16385e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251095} {:answer/id #uuid "997542b7-5b4e-5730-bcd9-42ca51f3257b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251871} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ebb09a-1202-54dc-96e3-4ba8aa79086d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252309} {:answer/id #uuid "d325e97e-1656-5db8-b154-544f8ba85d31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252423}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252309} :answer-field/id #uuid "49b60ab6-927a-5636-b89c-9078309c85cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ad2837f1-ee8d-5b88-b0b4-540909ba188a" :question/math-academy-id "q-11932" :question/problem "Given that $g(x)=ln⁡{x}^{2}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $g(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ng=ln⁡u,\\,u={x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cancel{x}}{x\\cdot \\cancel{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e29407f-0306-5cd7-ab50-d46e971435f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251071} {:answer/id #uuid "6218e58c-9107-5231-b02a-3a84de60083e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251349} {:answer/id #uuid "ae27a1dd-2895-5936-945a-8057f5eb72ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252071} {:answer/id #uuid "d57697f1-9470-5638-87e8-1592607aa161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252444} {:answer/id #uuid "f07f9d80-b3ae-5297-8430-2159434cec87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252656}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252071} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad77e15e-6b7f-5b66-be54-92af8304ca70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f206d2c2-ee8e-56e4-8de0-ea23491335cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-119379" :question/problem "$$\n\\frac{{\\operatorname{sin}}^{3}x{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}x+\\operatorname{sin}x{\\operatorname{cos}}^{4}x}{\\operatorname{cos}x\\operatorname{sin}x}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot 1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253580 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "236be099-00d2-5a93-807c-c0611363dd3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250857} {:answer/id #uuid "936b5a6a-37a9-599d-94c5-7ae7a2280c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251816} {:answer/id #uuid "b6bc72ad-8c01-5974-9602-15da4003854b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252163} {:answer/id #uuid "c9b770b1-d1d3-52d1-84af-ef96a46675ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252340} {:answer/id #uuid "cd8f375c-b6b5-5356-9e90-212803b05a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252366}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251816} :answer-field/id #uuid "42b3f8d2-ad82-503b-8cd5-80330391b6f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e1267137-e6ff-5440-b525-7d34538d465f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119451" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, and\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\frac{a-b\\sqrt{55}}{42},\n$$\n\ncalculate the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡u=1-{sin}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡u & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}\\right)}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{11})^{2}}{{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{11}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{36}-\\frac{11}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{36-11}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{36}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the first quadrant, where cosine is positive. So, we disregard the negative value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=\\frac{5}{6}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the sum formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{6}\\right)\\left(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)\\left(\\frac{2}{7}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{55}}{42}+\\frac{10}{42} \\\\  & =\\frac{10-3\\sqrt{55}}{42}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=10,b=3,$ and $a+b=13.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253598 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d321556-6d7c-5fd7-a04f-f5265f3a0a57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250670} {:answer/id #uuid "1b64a4c7-f36c-5305-b294-d6c4a3267f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250788} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9452f4-01d0-52e2-b147-a0fc90dcd6f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251318} {:answer/id #uuid "7b3fef91-949c-53e7-96aa-d706a95f608a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251578} {:answer/id #uuid "b12de12f-6e84-5959-8942-b6ce32ce6253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252102}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251318} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e030512-fec1-51e9-8560-0ce04304ec10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2e3715b1-99f4-58e2-8933-aec3faf54b69" :question/math-academy-id "q-11977" :question/problem "The Unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](images/68/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=4\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,2\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253608 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "070fdb32-1472-515e-90a7-b7eca04d4913" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =-9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250610} {:answer/id #uuid "a7f9142e-ec6a-5db4-bf53-b4b5f41ed070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-9$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252000} {:answer/id #uuid "bf5fecbe-8826-5f93-91a8-1a87c27225dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252242} {:answer/id #uuid "f168be24-e81a-5f01-8ba3-2fbfe874a9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-1$ and $\\lambda =-9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252663} {:answer/id #uuid "fb386fae-34fc-5885-8a54-f5b25dd5f4d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252755}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250610} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6fbb95b-fec0-59e1-80fd-da660864679f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3afe0de9-b343-5b36-b1d3-181e3380faa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-11984" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle M=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $M-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nM-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-4-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(M-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-4-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 5 & -4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-4-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )-5\\cdot 5 & =0 \\\\ 16+4\\lambda +4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-25 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda -9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{{8}^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 9}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{100}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm 10}{2} \\\\  & =1,-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =-9.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253616 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4719a11c-b592-520f-92dc-489d374471db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251143} {:answer/id #uuid "59c91c19-f570-5aa8-816c-cc0cb1075be7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251291} {:answer/id #uuid "59ce9bf3-76f3-54c2-bcfa-870a4e3b1a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251292} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf9dc73-33a3-5ec1-9101-2f6f9ab08b0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251449} {:answer/id #uuid "f36a72e2-2ba4-5339-933f-dd6199828644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252688}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251143} :answer-field/id #uuid "01723d61-511b-58d2-a534-8acc9358fdf0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7b2a7a5d-5ff3-58b1-bc1e-3ba374a0cda5" :question/math-academy-id "q-119863" :question/problem "$\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the numerator using $1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡x}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253617 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00677872-7616-5c6b-bc06-e85a41bca0b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250553} {:answer/id #uuid "60dff4f9-0626-5330-99dd-f03bb2eb6f7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251345} {:answer/id #uuid "a43f7607-4390-56c0-ba26-6beaa6359216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251971} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc2c36b-5bb0-5f2e-8ad7-e904eb5d214b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252208} {:answer/id #uuid "bc732a44-7bfc-58d9-95fa-404ba29a3bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252217}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252208} :answer-field/id #uuid "68996742-5572-5673-a555-2490c8c236c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a1b437a5-869a-5ccd-aeb4-884c52b20f38" :question/math-academy-id "q-119864" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the numerator using $1-{sin}^{2}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1}=\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the numerator as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1} & =\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}}{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1} \\\\  & =-(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1}=-(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253618 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1588e060-eaf7-5910-9e61-b0aee1f7f521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250739} {:answer/id #uuid "494ac200-c612-57c9-b672-67e5fd17b71e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251164} {:answer/id #uuid "8294f538-53f1-5624-815b-68ab1cc8f31a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251654} {:answer/id #uuid "ee5dbf1c-7a22-5698-b16f-9495dc61f07e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252640} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4a8bae-9aa0-5b9a-ba6e-2bd82ca874f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252757}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252640} :answer-field/id #uuid "e33eb130-9aa7-52d1-9cc8-68e09e60cbc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8e68dcc2-8781-5eb7-a08a-4c11847234f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119866" :question/problem "$\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)^{2}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the denominator using $1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)^{2}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)^{2}}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the denominator as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)^{2}}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)}{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)\\cancel{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)}}{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cancel{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253619 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c53ae73-683c-5a2f-b267-532610f58dda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250792} {:answer/id #uuid "33c8224e-d240-5f4e-93a7-ebbcaec62640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250985} {:answer/id #uuid "a34cbf62-878a-5094-9a13-a1580cea4a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251959} {:answer/id #uuid "a4c335cf-6e50-556d-8e8b-d579292a8d87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251974} {:answer/id #uuid "d959dcd8-2950-558a-8ad2-c452dab5edbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252469}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250985} :answer-field/id #uuid "e822311d-ffa4-5b0b-a925-5497895eff61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "af3d18fb-a784-53a2-9372-1a3bbb7ca376" :question/math-academy-id "q-119867" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the numerator of the first term using $1-{sin}^{2}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the numerator of the first term as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253620 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "036caea1-1921-5d22-9547-552db4e0d7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250581} {:answer/id #uuid "6c9302db-ed98-5640-9305-d59856cde305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-(2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251446} {:answer/id #uuid "9fadc601-d5a2-58de-b48f-3c1587b3edb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251927} {:answer/id #uuid "d723301e-e03b-5302-8be0-9fa545ceba62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252462} {:answer/id #uuid "e3604fe1-47f9-5dda-bb6a-0c434776fcf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252554}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252462} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cef525e-df3e-5d3b-8f88-3906fd36659e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fe39df04-92b7-5f70-a2a5-5ed05c5e127c" :question/math-academy-id "q-119869" :question/problem "If $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{2{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{1}{f(x)},\n$$ then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the denominator using $1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{2{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{2(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the denominator as difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{2(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}{2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{2\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-2(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253621 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27f0a8ce-4aec-512b-a809-fe80d7a37254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡z+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250896} {:answer/id #uuid "383e056a-7d1a-580d-8144-5ce601bf73a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-2{cot}^{2}⁡z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251020} {:answer/id #uuid "449a0196-c334-57cc-9c6b-f43d1c3715ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{cot}^{2}⁡z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251123} {:answer/id #uuid "978b01e0-91fd-53a4-93a7-f12af31fb3e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{cot}^{2}⁡z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251854} {:answer/id #uuid "d552fd33-bdd6-5221-8186-0acd1c018978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{cot}^{2}⁡z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252441}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251854} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3ef446b-20ba-56ee-b042-97aed74369c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d3d698d1-fddf-50d2-9b5a-51d1e576d1b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-119904" :question/problem "Simplify ${cos}^{2}⁡z\\,({cot}^{2}⁡z+1).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡z={csc}^{2}⁡z,$ we rewrite and simplify the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡z\\,({cot}^{2}⁡z+1) & ={cos}^{2}⁡z\\cdot {csc}^{2}⁡z \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡z\\cdot {\\left(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\\right)}^{2} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡z\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡z} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡z}{{sin}^{2}⁡z} \\\\  & ={\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡z}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\\right)}^{2} \\\\  & ={cot}^{2}⁡z\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253622 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d5b7420-54f3-5900-b0a3-79f8fbb0ed3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250799} {:answer/id #uuid "751e1635-7363-5b19-8dbe-a67e6a8709a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251518} {:answer/id #uuid "a8803e4a-e94e-5c17-b524-28d591c30402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252012} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d6050e-5c66-503f-b94d-d7319de6c00c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252173} {:answer/id #uuid "fa98dcfb-2b88-54da-a7a9-14c4a5590e71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252749}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252749} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2d89d63-0ffd-537e-9d8f-e71866db7a14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "06466b4b-c6cd-5178-abe2-7bb6034e59d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119905" :question/problem "Simplify ${sin}^{2}⁡w\\,(1+{cot}^{2}⁡w).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡w={csc}^{2}⁡w,$ we rewrite and simplify the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡w\\,(1+{cot}^{2}⁡w) & ={sin}^{2}⁡w\\cdot {csc}^{2}⁡w \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡w\\cdot {\\left(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡w}\\right)}^{2} \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡w\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡w} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d5c33db-f615-52b7-9136-0d1e8a15743a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250800} {:answer/id #uuid "4c697a58-e888-53e3-8497-2a49e654fe69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251187} {:answer/id #uuid "a7142337-e88f-526b-957f-ff25c2d67729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251993} {:answer/id #uuid "f13b2e10-8763-5954-9ba6-493b24c00f7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252660} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e11755-0e5a-53d5-8480-4af6a0eed93c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252732}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252732} :answer-field/id #uuid "94835c25-f561-5105-9df4-57d4e1017aed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "67f941a8-74c6-537b-aaa1-feb29dbe709f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119906" :question/problem "Simplify $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ we rewrite and simplify the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253629 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9091e145-d5e4-58db-9a8e-4ce061fcd0f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251784} {:answer/id #uuid "aab6294d-67a7-58a9-aabd-cc0882409576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252031} {:answer/id #uuid "b330bc65-41bf-59e9-a350-941037eb07c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252120} {:answer/id #uuid "f3dbf917-e612-5719-99c8-5cfd2f0c0af9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252691} {:answer/id #uuid "fa7138d3-5d87-57fc-b931-ce18940eaf7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252747}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252691} :answer-field/id #uuid "db5fec58-f806-5ed1-8146-72c007a4dcf9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "83d0963d-a8db-5840-a576-ccf3c21b5f89" :question/math-academy-id "q-120020" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)$ in the numerator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253632 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a1adf34-b5ab-575a-b655-c479f3717df6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250640} {:answer/id #uuid "199a6b8d-c1b5-52ec-8d2b-338601436874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250776} {:answer/id #uuid "38546a08-184f-5411-80ea-0b9a2a403009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251022} {:answer/id #uuid "65f52443-c286-5605-b6f6-ab3d3b725230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251392} {:answer/id #uuid "e2a2c78e-06dc-539e-b4e5-76443acce72b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252545}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250640} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0d401dc-d0fa-51c1-b8e5-f54d86918a91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "df53af64-a7fb-5920-a9ae-4765f5d7236c" :question/math-academy-id "q-120029" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{100}^{∘}\\operatorname{tan}⁡{50}^{∘}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={50}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {50}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({100}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{100}^{∘}\\operatorname{tan}⁡{50}^{∘}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing  the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}=1-{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} & =\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})}{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253633 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f5c4341-844a-577b-b58f-76df8e5a0650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251768} {:answer/id #uuid "985ce000-4fea-5dc8-9935-4982a6d889a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{140}^{∘}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251862} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e93ea9-7881-550e-ad03-b9b187cb54dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{140}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252015} {:answer/id #uuid "e50ef96f-52d4-5e2f-914d-d92cc5e4c4cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252559} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b6f3c0-5e40-55c9-b6ff-cb6efa4d0891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252708}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251768} :answer-field/id #uuid "a44df084-3230-5ebb-a9f5-baf76119a7b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "20492e7a-2ad5-5346-9935-34abf42dcea6" :question/math-academy-id "q-120030" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{140}^{∘}\\operatorname{cot}⁡{70}^{∘}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={70}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {70}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{140}^{∘}\\operatorname{cot}⁡{70}^{∘}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing  the Pythagorean identity in the form ${cos}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘}=1-{sin}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2(1-{sin}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘})}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})\\cancel{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})}}{\\cancel{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253641 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "053f36b4-6fc7-536b-8778-64782d3f6eec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{cot}^{4}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250595} {:answer/id #uuid "740ebbd9-73c4-5313-a752-c21a1a2a65b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251510} {:answer/id #uuid "aa6d64e1-5758-5