)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254547} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2ff8db-4995-5531-9ef6-10f0585e85d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254923} {:answer/id #uuid "96f239ff-4f7d-598d-ae07-5b24ea0f2611" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254999} {:answer/id #uuid "e192abdb-22ab-5b4e-8e0e-96f4a4dc0ee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255671} {:answer/id #uuid "fed61b56-63c6-54aa-84e0-91cc6d252edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255910}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255671} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f82915f-10ef-56ab-829a-4cb0e79eacbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6bb4ecb6-0b76-51e4-aa33-5be6f12e1dbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-120347" :question/problem "Express $$\n\\displaystyle 2{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\n$$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n2({cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)-{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right))\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)-{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)-{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256393 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05d4fe96-e437-5459-b90d-0a3bdfc1825d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253714} {:answer/id #uuid "60f62d48-049d-5a6d-a9e6-66749d676bd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254537} {:answer/id #uuid "988c0b62-37ae-5848-98ed-b1e6c7c32632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255019} {:answer/id #uuid "a00792a6-ab66-5c63-99fe-0e99a6d1bfd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255080} {:answer/id #uuid "d0cd2ac8-79c2-55c9-8923-9989a38dea95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255532}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255532} :answer-field/id #uuid "88f8237f-b76a-5905-b3b4-ed1d154b073e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cf1faff6-afe0-59ea-a58f-f8289c637840" :question/math-academy-id "q-120348" :question/problem "Express $\\sqrt{3}{cos}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}-\\sqrt{3}{sin}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}({cos}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={35}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {35}^{∘})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}({cos}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘})=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256394 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ce3d726-77ed-56ed-b5e7-178b2ec95a63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{38}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254332} {:answer/id #uuid "7b1c8631-9160-52f9-ac15-c3e9d435ff8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{76}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254764} {:answer/id #uuid "876d3930-aa82-505d-9f8e-ac1e75af8bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{76}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254871} {:answer/id #uuid "a02d4e42-7793-5fce-a84e-fa7ada0f721d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{76}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255081} {:answer/id #uuid "c891ae38-c980-596c-afb6-21d0fdf24cfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{38}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255456}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186254764} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4536025-00cb-5226-bad7-2557200ad84c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256219}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a4d26858-a337-5218-af76-0e3d4aac3fca" :question/math-academy-id "q-120352" :question/problem "Express $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{5}{2}{cos}^{2}⁡{38}^{∘}-\\frac{5}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡{38}^{∘}\n$$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{2}({cos}^{2}⁡{38}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡