"$U=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "87b20497-ceac-5d64-8634-616821707ef5" :question/math-academy-id "q-127757" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $S$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(S)=1\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 0=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(S)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $S$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot (-6)-4\\cdot (-3)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)=0,$ we conclude that $T$ is not invertible. Since $T$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $T$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $U$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(U)=0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1)=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(U)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $U$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $T$ is singular."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262825 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d30b47ef-87b0-5e27-a184-0a096fd33124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463652} {:answer/id #uuid "33d939ee-6d35-51bf-8bb9-1d48cd53e796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463653}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463653} :answer-field/id #uuid "13f6015b-077b-5764-a2dd-d3aae8b43612" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4af08d0a-5536-510f-abab-da5fdbdceb28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463654} {:answer/id #uuid "35d0cb07-478b-566b-9247-784f753b25b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463655}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #e