c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-236" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263674} {:answer/id #uuid "597beba5-ebc1-5875-b8bc-e7d0f915a765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-224" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263768} {:answer/id #uuid "84f97719-93d5-5bc8-bb1d-4514159fc0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-260" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264143}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264143} :answer-field/id #uuid "2be5b7b1-6bce-50a0-9ce6-981e62f75674" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "315e2903-a515-5453-992e-2f5084f6607a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130497" :question/problem "Given that $$\n\\displaystyle C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ find $det(C).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}6\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(8-18)\\cdot (36-10) \\\\  & =(-10)\\cdot 26 \\\\  & =-260.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265948 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36f304f8-92e8-51a7-b162-d70782a1c348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263492} {:answer/id #uuid "3ad553e1-5759-5c80-aea1-b19a2c528e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263524} {:answer/id #uuid "5c396193-d1e2-5c07-ab21-8ee06b268902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263794} {:answer/id #uuid "60eb6a69-4e31-5fd0-8238-b39bcb055083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263837} {:answer/id #uuid "616d3a76-1bf3-5317-9871-b368f9f8170b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263841}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263794} :answer-field/id #uuid "f29ff58d-9c44-54c2-82fc-6274cfaab393" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0bc36fde-175a-5a60-bfe0-4edee290223c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130631" :question/problem "Let $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ be square matrices. If $A=B\\cdot C,$  $|B|=-15$ and $|{C}^{-1}|=3$, find $|A|.$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nAlso, given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $M,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({M}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(M)}.\n$$\n\nSince $|C|=\\frac{1}{|{C}^{-1}|}$, we get $|C|=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|B|\\cdot |C| \\\\  & =(-15)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265957 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2528ad02-5f9f-56ea-8410-d39c904636dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263319} {:answer/id #uuid "362ac5c7-47e1-5e9d-8da7-99af33e68594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263480} {:answer/id #uuid "4fa78b20-3f5d-55c8-86ed-4c78587bb1c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263692} {:answer/id #uuid "a3218cf6-888a-5cda-afec-e72dd2c490c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264382} {:answer/id #uuid "a671b3df-f73e-52a5-abad-23025e5c9057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264424}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263692} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f07356d-1b59-583c-af54-685c269168f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c7e6dfda-559d-5807-8c00-15f567ac0047" :question/math-academy-id "q-130678" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=-15.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{5}$ (switching the first and the fifth rows). What is the value of $det(B)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =-det(A) \\\\  & =-(-15) \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265958 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fc73746-5ea9-55f8-b808-29feb76310d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263144} {:answer/id #uuid "1903197b-94a5-5ae8-8488-ea9189ba7a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263238} {:answer/id #uuid "401520f0-03ac-5a9b-84d6-a131ab139fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263567} {:answer/id #uuid "4c24dd35-c22b-52a4-81e6-5ceeb7c1f1ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263658} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d562f2-dc14-5de9-9168-e664e9f871b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264851}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263238} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a7b7f5a-0e83-5b65-b31f-11b8ca8d3de0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "21413729-993b-5951-9f65-5a6557f13d10" :question/math-academy-id "q-130682" :question/problem "Suppose $X$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(X)=55.$ The matrix $Y$ is obtained from $X$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{3}$ (switching the fifth and the third rows). What is the value of $det(Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(55) \\\\  & =-55.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265963 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "286e6c23-07b7-5545-a441-9b04e008b90e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263350} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6428b7-cec3-5983-8fd4-6d5bfd014e11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263662} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2b9105-1dc5-57ef-87e1-d54b08b77a89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263689} {:answer/id #uuid "d25edb74-8a68-5d7d-8761-5cc2ad370bc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264834} {:answer/id #uuid "f485bfa8-3aea-5a28-ac04-0ce06bbcbe24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265146}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263350} :answer-field/id #uuid "83755a28-ab8b-5aef-9021-ec305e4c871e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e4a32b49-da98-512a-a647-8bab7fd6db7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130732" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(A)=-63.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{2}{9}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{2}{9}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =\\frac{2}{9}det(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot (-63) \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eea86b0-9537-5bab-868c-813e628926c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263556} {:answer/id #uuid "bd11cc58-68f3-5442-86d9-2ca462bc2de3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264640} {:answer/id #uuid "c560179e-32df-53c2-bf75-91bcf107dd87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264730} {:answer/id #uuid "ea98ec76-cd9c-58ef-9dd7-1b6b68c939e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265044} {:answer/id #uuid "efe386fa-5a31-5644-9aef-ffa3e5a0fe23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265107}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264730} :answer-field/id #uuid "39bcf4c6-cfb1-5621-8688-276a463c7247" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4e651dd5-d08c-5af1-84eb-5024fff39147" :question/math-academy-id "q-130733" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=200.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{6}:=\\frac{3}{50}{R}_{6}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $B$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{3}{50}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{3}{50}det(B) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{50}\\cdot 200 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f43edac-7246-5d43-8000-c3bbff4a8176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263825} {:answer/id #uuid "86e0a75e-55d0-5e2a-9a63-a82c9c202c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264165} {:answer/id #uuid "baa05d38-6ecb-5379-9f1f-5e3e7b9ccf4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264618} {:answer/id #uuid "d4349a15-8511-5f32-95bd-1870e7829de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264848} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0308d4-84ec-5efb-85f8-99f4481efc31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265234}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264848} :answer-field/id #uuid "c44403e8-a5cd-5235-983a-00f2ee10a5ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "06a215a3-28a1-5081-94e6-eb4defb995c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-130738" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(B)=-3.$ What is the value of $det(-2B)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot B)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=-2$ and $n=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(-2B) & =(-2)^{5}\\cdot det(B) \\\\  & =-32\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =96.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265966 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ea955b9-6711-5c65-bda1-3ab48eabd812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263132} {:answer/id #uuid "17da9e59-b9f5-509b-a7fb-62f252a7e9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263226} {:answer/id #uuid "33f0d4df-6db7-5edb-83e5-879e71782b3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263453} {:answer/id #uuid "6565e424-45a3-596a-a6bd-d07a0bf5686e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263879} {:answer/id #uuid "95a19408-ad9c-5d73-b520-d5ebea3b4631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264282}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263453} :answer-field/id #uuid "304a5032-001d-525b-8f6a-528d675f38d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6d71a2d5-21fb-5641-ae6e-b88e302c6622" :question/math-academy-id "q-130739" :question/problem "Suppose $Y$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(Y)=2.$ What is the value of $det(-4Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot Y)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(Y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=-4$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(-4Y) & =(-4)^{3}\\cdot det(Y) \\\\  & =-64\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-128.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265967 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "121a0910-0c84-5231-bdd6-25a30f65897a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263167} {:answer/id #uuid "2c80c122-c6fb-5d05-9845-b09ffeb4eb3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263376} {:answer/id #uuid "39934266-8c1f-5d45-a413-a141d9ef5e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263512} {:answer/id #uuid "64f7903d-1ae5-5db3-bcd2-250d5107b78d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "250" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263873} {:answer/id #uuid "e1d3804a-dea0-5e00-8325-d6ee1dd1097a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "175" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264960}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263376} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0ae65f4-2ac2-5397-ad79-04f3366a06c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2a9423ed-dddc-5ecd-95fd-6191f18eab23" :question/math-academy-id "q-130740" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(B)=-4.$ What is the value of $det(5B)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot B)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=5$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(5B) & ={5}^{2}\\cdot det(B) \\\\  & =25\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-100.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265968 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48b73141-d30a-51a6-9f59-931d33013ea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263625} {:answer/id #uuid "4dc874e1-0a0a-51b3-b460-40ba95dc7640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263673} {:answer/id #uuid "b49f38a2-031f-51dc-8877-a5a624bb1218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264552} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ac9249-0666-5a46-986f-2eafc3fc9b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264745} {:answer/id #uuid "f48bc418-eacd-5a87-a261-84a9526488c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265147}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264745} :answer-field/id #uuid "df63d5a1-1430-5bfe-a708-b9a8006ddea4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265638}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e4056ea9-ab56-5308-af07-58d0dddfaa0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130741" :question/problem "Suppose $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(C)=-5,$ What is the value of $det(4C)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot C)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=4$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(4C) & ={4}^{2}\\cdot det(C) \\\\  & =16\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-80.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a0f29de-25aa-5107-8046-0dd732f9beb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263097} {:answer/id #uuid "162deb0b-2730-571d-b037-7db47a3aea46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263209} {:answer/id #uuid "1b8f75e2-26ce-5967-ac8a-f06080423598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263259} {:answer/id #uuid "66de9e61-f678-5f09-92fa-20666c0a4a57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263891} {:answer/id #uuid "f578aa5a-7ba5-5a91-8942-93f38512c9ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265150}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263097} :answer-field/id #uuid "f00b119d-2bbd-5aff-88de-546820f3c832" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "da7f3dfc-3649-55d6-80af-942a6a83828d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130767" :question/problem "Suppose $X$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(X)=28.$ The matrix $Y$ is obtained from $X$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{3}{4}{R}_{1}$ and ${R}_{6}:={R}_{6}+(-7){R}_{2}.$ What is the value of $det(Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{6}:={R}_{6}+(-7){R}_{2}$ involves adding a multiple of one row to another row,  so it does not change the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{3}{4}{R}_{1}$ involves multiplying a row by $\\frac{3}{4},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $\\frac{3}{4}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we only have to multiply the determinant by $\\frac{3}{4}.$ Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =\\frac{3}{4}det(X) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 28 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c504d34-49a8-5293-9654-9bb371251af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263118} {:answer/id #uuid "668e2da3-ac3d-5bec-b6b1-16504c2d81fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263886} {:answer/id #uuid "7573103e-73e5-56e6-832d-af6582780369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264021} {:answer/id #uuid "90344634-d8cd-51fb-85d7-7f08481a8bde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264236} {:answer/id #uuid "c168c56a-3c78-5c71-873d-48190da505aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264678}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264236} :answer-field/id #uuid "37455212-8943-576e-a134-59b320488bd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b71bc5d0-3557-578c-8a3d-25da59fcce16" :question/math-academy-id "q-130771" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=-75.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ and ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ involves multiplying a row by $\\frac{4}{5},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-det(B)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}det(B) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-75) \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d8f1dd-9c61-582a-91cb-1b1b14e544ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263489} {:answer/id #uuid "7cfe718c-c4c1-5e05-a605-9f1eeeec4a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264078} {:answer/id #uuid "b62d6a25-1160-5e5d-826d-11092cfa8fd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264579} {:answer/id #uuid "ee61c6e2-7ebd-5d28-8d0e-3007260e4c30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265084} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a2f26a-317b-5119-9e11-1fcf1b2dfd40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265123}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263489} :answer-field/id #uuid "eab97c28-5a65-571d-9829-1e7bb5397bea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265662}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7d54eadd-5171-5d74-9872-72cd2ba1ef45" :question/math-academy-id "q-130843" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f938576-14ee-5665-942c-f5bfc3534050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263289} {:answer/id #uuid "66e265c6-ed48-5d88-966e-a5dff8678916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263892} {:answer/id #uuid "96934c85-fbb8-5687-a238-dbee446961d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264288} {:answer/id #uuid "a3c6c16d-b28c-5665-bfd2-d38f6dbf5091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264392} {:answer/id #uuid "d5476105-e8e0-591e-9f16-19d7dff3433b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264857}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264392} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d92ecd7-28e6-5f20-bfc3-d836c30d39c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a88eab2f-0bec-591e-a119-0d1e91654bf5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130854" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5631a190-3164-5c81-9c22-e6a70c44c09d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263742} {:answer/id #uuid "74e1b546-dc5d-5c39-8615-b03158b816ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264014} {:answer/id #uuid "850ef7c7-1f4b-53c9-b078-25bda4009629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264145} {:answer/id #uuid "df7141db-3b66-5a7a-b89e-874dcb0bbee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264937} {:answer/id #uuid "e044d557-77d9-53d0-a554-77b04c1a4a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264947}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264014} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf6cdcea-ffe0-5e06-a7c5-0284d3815f01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2e099506-9b8a-52ad-a7eb-ff6f42b6d002" :question/math-academy-id "q-130855" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $X$ and $Y$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(X)=5$, find $det(Y).$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $Y$ can be obtained from $X$ by swapping the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(5) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c90d582-f52e-5c66-95e3-3ad844320816" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263119} {:answer/id #uuid "5e529ace-2bd8-58f0-986c-1e4d9c74356d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263816} {:answer/id #uuid "a65dd175-ee5d-5d8d-9f0d-5f2b7ace68d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264423} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4db568-3851-57c1-97bf-ea269c62e7ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264629} {:answer/id #uuid "c4faeda8-6e8c-52b3-8a7f-01f15c3fc3cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264727}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264423} :answer-field/id #uuid "daab1c93-d290-5e33-a7b6-21310d1db988" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f6af6cd7-62fa-5e02-a671-191adf935b8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130857" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $X$ and $Y$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(X)=-60$, find $det(Y).$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $Y$ can be obtained from $X$ by swapping the $1$st and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(-60) \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266045 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "254608a3-f4c4-524d-bdd6-4734ea7a9ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263322} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca6a3f0-0a99-59ca-89a0-00d1f53a84ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263935} {:answer/id #uuid "848415f8-f9ee-573e-9e2c-e1517406f8f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264137} {:answer/id #uuid "9205aebe-b2d8-5a93-8a96-975a2e76b5c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264250} {:answer/id #uuid "e0fb479c-83a3-5744-99c8-93b5e83e4668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264955}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264955} :answer-field/id #uuid "4716f2cc-0f74-549d-b0ab-845a4315cc85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265379}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "984e49ec-1c3a-575d-8328-f0b575ca3b17" :question/math-academy-id "q-131096" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle D=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & ={d}_{11}{C}_{11}+{d}_{12}{C}_{12}+{d}_{13}{C}_{13}+{d}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+1\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =1{C}_{14} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}1} \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 6 & 5 & 3 & {\\color{lightgray}∗}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(-1)^{1+4}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-1\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =-(0-4(3\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 6)+0) \\\\  & =-48\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266046 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33a08f51-b677-5b68-ba7a-dac3baa9eb2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263449} {:answer/id #uuid "6b51c736-ffe0-52cf-a537-2dbf8f99b091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{31}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263926} {:answer/id #uuid "86e76cd7-4277-5294-92f3-131eaa99845a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264166} {:answer/id #uuid "ae7b46e1-3b32-525c-ad19-743406d4fd14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "115" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264501} {:answer/id #uuid "f10b6e0e-0a43-5cd2-aaf1-18a085bf0628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265117}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263449} :answer-field/id #uuid "310e57cf-52eb-56bb-88ee-20cd79122820" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ec31df61-abd0-5be5-8c6f-e699fba92ddd" :question/math-academy-id "q-131114" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle Z=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Z) & ={z}_{11}{C}_{11}+{z}_{12}{C}_{12}+{z}_{13}{C}_{13}+{z}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{C}_{11} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}\\frac{1}{2}} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 5 & 3 & 2 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 2 & 3 & 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0+2(5\\cdot 8-2\\cdot 2)+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 72 \\\\  & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ad7fbd-daaf-5638-b84c-e71398abac22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263153} {:answer/id #uuid "1bafca79-f3d5-5d3c-94b1-acb828f5d148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "99" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263260} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf09706-5715-5579-bf1d-d65287fd8c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263666} {:answer/id #uuid "d4648e08-8d5c-5a1c-9f99-ddecfd09c9a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264849} {:answer/id #uuid "f09fabd2-0746-5418-a46d-e35f208be02e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265110}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263260} :answer-field/id #uuid "79a1e1f3-7831-5686-8eed-cf31e6adf808" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265451}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "868d3e09-dc03-51a5-9f3e-bb57d096be39" :question/math-academy-id "q-131122" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle W=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(W) & ={w}_{11}{C}_{11}+{w}_{12}{C}_{12}+{w}_{13}{C}_{13}+{w}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+2\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =-{C}_{12}+2{C}_{14} \\\\  & =-1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}-1} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 3 & 6\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}2} \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & {\\color{lightgray}∗}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-1\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot (-1)^{4+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix}+1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-2\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =9-2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =9+90 \\\\  & =99\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266049 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dfdbbd1-5a22-5fac-b1e2-3afe6c40ce0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263676} {:answer/id #uuid "55f5d0f8-a672-555a-a9fc-13c54562ca11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263740} {:answer/id #uuid "bdb209a5-aa3e-5b55-a77c-6f8d24ec3380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264648} {:answer/id #uuid "eadc0e14-599f-56be-8b29-dcb4146bb189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265046} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a8de52-0682-5310-813f-8db91b654bb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265177}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265046} :answer-field/id #uuid "15c91375-19ab-565d-8c35-c44e7cc346df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4e01c006-ae42-500a-b8c8-9322bf670a47" :question/math-academy-id "q-131123" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle H=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(H) & ={h}_{11}{C}_{11}+{h}_{12}{C}_{12}+{h}_{13}{C}_{13}+{h}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+1\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & ={C}_{12}-{C}_{14} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}1} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 & 8 \\\\ 1 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}-1} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & {\\color{lightgray}∗}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{4+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+8\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\right)+\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-1)+(-3)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-8-3 \\\\  & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "074a7b07-1dde-5c0e-b2f1-1df5849345fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263065} {:answer/id #uuid "2696b949-990f-53f5-9757-20ab22a560fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263337} {:answer/id #uuid "7175a500-4328-5795-aaae-15fb7825a197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263982} {:answer/id #uuid "a366480c-97d9-558f-b732-c0cee3515a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264386} {:answer/id #uuid "cb3102a8-a3e1-572a-b462-5aaa095924ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264779}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263065} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2f6375b-0373-52ae-b2df-a2db6871f3be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265564}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fb96bf60-dce3-5654-ba59-509a2507fee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-131225" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter $t.$ Since we are given the curve $r(t)$ parametrized by the parameter $t$ (not the arc length $s$), we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{tan}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sec}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t}⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19a5c0af-c4ce-5f99-9235-d587f027c666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+xz+2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263244} {:answer/id #uuid "50c3b86c-2856-5dfd-b4cc-b0210233a03d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263701} {:answer/id #uuid "86edd1c6-b12c-57d6-bea1-1bb8eb59a573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "yz\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264167} {:answer/id #uuid "a5091070-cf3d-5e35-9bdc-407d30f58fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "xyz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+xz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264410} {:answer/id #uuid "df321538-2950-56a6-86ef-8cb6a8380270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+x{z}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264935}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263701} :answer-field/id #uuid "42d61a01-eacf-5108-b43b-c7d0f51fc8de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "78be230d-a8c8-5e13-ad01-df6f6ca0d5f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-131298" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y,z)=⟨\\frac{4}{y}{sin}^{2}⁡z,x{z}^{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡z⟩$ and $f(x,y,z)=xy+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨y,x,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡z⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4}{y}{sin}^{2}⁡z)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{z}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =(xy+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡z+⟨\\frac{4}{y}{sin}^{2}⁡z,x{z}^{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡z⟩\\cdot ⟨y,x,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+2{cos}^{2}⁡z+4{sin}^{2}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}-2{sin}^{2}⁡z \\\\  & =xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2({sin}^{2}⁡z+{cos}^{2}⁡z) \\\\  & =xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266075 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15bbc91c-fd98-5b6c-9665-d70f774533af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+xy{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}-xz{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263203} {:answer/id #uuid "525a85d8-be7f-5e58-9de9-1e1199f1635c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+xy{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+xz{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263710} {:answer/id #uuid "80f54f21-e7c4-5ec3-b1d5-b02fa7b3c8dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+xy{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}-xz{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264109} {:answer/id #uuid "c704cdce-34fa-5e66-8fcd-a5d31c4900df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(x{e}^{yz}-z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+x{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}-xz{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264741} {:answer/id #uuid "fd353914-244d-5acb-856d-77f4123cb4ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(xy{e}^{yz}-z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}-{x}^{2}{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265224}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263203} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcd0b969-143e-57e9-a012-fd5218ecced7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2c3cbbe9-4c45-5e2a-804f-38b6dd4503b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-131336" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=x{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+yz\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k},$ what is $\\text{curl}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{F}?$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{F}=P\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+Q\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+R\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}$ is a vector field on ${\\mathbb{R}}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $\\mathbf{F}$ all exist, then the curl of $\\mathbf{F}$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{F}=\\mathrm{∇}\\times \\mathbf{F}=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{F} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ x{e}^{yz} & yz & {e}^{yz}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{yz})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz)]\\mathbf{i}-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{yz})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{e}^{yz})]\\mathbf{j}+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{yz})]\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-(0-xy{e}^{yz})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(0-xz{e}^{yz})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+xy{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}-xz{e}^{yz}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266122 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5eb19a9f-9048-5bd2-9825-48b46c374012" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263819} {:answer/id #uuid "6b1b9851-e23d-5c89-85c7-166c2502e4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263923} {:answer/id #uuid "792aef7e-fcea-560d-8fb8-5bfd5fef2507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264051} {:answer/id #uuid "d64da940-c21b-5ec2-8ac3-b32049952204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264863} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb74e9b-1c1a-510f-8253-e0339f0362f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265089}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265089} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cc15e45-edbf-58cf-997c-64f5fe6f3649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c55df30b-b976-5e8f-92e6-7035630c5b16" :question/math-academy-id "q-131931" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right),\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right),\\frac{\\sqrt{5}s}{3}⟩,\\,0\\le s\\le 4\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}s}{3}\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right),\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right),\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right),\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-\\frac{1}{3}|\\cdot \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right)+{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right)+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266123 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "060e8ac7-c2dd-583e-8cd4-269668a1bd65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263053} {:answer/id #uuid "5bd5cc43-f5be-54d4-a853-918f93243c3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263791} {:answer/id #uuid "7e266b8c-6204-5308-b98b-75df403969e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264089} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a9be4e-ada8-5ff7-9e40-aab3c770d443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264708} {:answer/id #uuid "e3363089-5b0b-58fe-8d13-8582775bc371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264973}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263053} :answer-field/id #uuid "310c8278-a1fd-50c6-98a6-247ab7fab855" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2753f58b-fd37-5228-8b91-aed9f3f510a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-131938" :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s⟩,\\,0\\le s\\le \\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s⟩ \\\\  & =-3⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-3|\\cdot \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡3s+{sin}^{2}⁡3s} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18914e3b-4c0c-57aa-b830-1660863a7e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{2}+2}{{t}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263233} {:answer/id #uuid "5f58c6ad-9319-5d1b-9d99-ea47c8f0a8bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263826} {:answer/id #uuid "80ef917a-5f07-5b72-a464-1b7b07712278" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2{t}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264108} {:answer/id #uuid "be495737-6290-535e-adb2-48549199f663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{2}+2}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264653} {:answer/id #uuid "e9d65c24-d2d2-5f84-a217-8a8e9701cc32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{2}+2}{({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265035}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265035} :answer-field/id #uuid "33500533-1ff2-52fe-b070-b355792f8c8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7eb005e4-b7c8-57e9-a9a3-c7cb18e5c9e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-132067" :question/problem "Using the cross product curvature formula, find the curvature of $r(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ as a function of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0⟩\\times ⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 0 \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{vmatrix}\\,k \\\\  & =[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)]k \\\\  & =[2{cos}^{2}⁡t-3t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t+2{sin}^{2}⁡t+3t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t]k \\\\  & =(2({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+{t}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t))k \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+2)k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖={t}^{2}+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}+2}{{(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1})}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}+2}{({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266134 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f6b0400-1e68-5781-99dd-baf4bf29f183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263136} {:answer/id #uuid "138465c2-a944-5f69-a306-dbe0d9e9957b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263184} {:answer/id #uuid "448c181d-6900-569e-9449-e68a2b27fbbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263601} {:answer/id #uuid "454b974a-3a5e-5fee-86d8-8896d99f85a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263609} {:answer/id #uuid "7a55c469-2f19-5c4e-b637-d06464759dd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264061}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263609} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b54510a-b668-5df8-bf78-4080c1b6ef70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1ac67b14-8558-510c-8d38-cf5ff7d90671" :question/math-academy-id "q-132105" :question/problem "Consider a curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s.$ Find the radius of curvature of $r(s)$ at an arbitrary point knowing that its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are both parametrized by arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{κ(s)}=\\frac{1}{‖{T}^{′}(s)‖}\n$$\n\nWe differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and calculate its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(s)‖ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}+{(-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡s+{cos}^{2}⁡s+2{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡s+2{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2({cos}^{2}⁡s+{sin}^{2}⁡s)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{‖{T}^{′}(s)‖}=\\frac{1}{1}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266135 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "565fcbf8-c589-5729-80a1-0ddccc1d0e4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263745} {:answer/id #uuid "8c3a0e69-772d-50a6-b0fe-a3acb3d20ce2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4{s}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264199} {:answer/id #uuid "972f0bca-1fc3-504e-affd-f755b418fdc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264294} {:answer/id #uuid "98c16e91-b1be-577d-a576-6f50e0dd91e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264313} {:answer/id #uuid "b8bde1fb-b76d-5fa2-940c-bc8f4b3d1e8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264600}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264313} :answer-field/id #uuid "b78b1b42-52ba-5f1a-86c0-3f790b5bb698" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265568}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f5eb3832-8b64-51ad-af13-7886aea1f298" :question/math-academy-id "q-132110" :question/problem "Consider a curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s.$ Find the radius of curvature of $r(s)$ at an arbitrary point knowing that its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,\\sqrt{3}⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are both parametrized by arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{κ(s)}=\\frac{1}{‖{T}^{′}(s)‖}\n$$\n\nWe differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and calculate its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{3})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s}}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s}}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(s)‖ & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s})}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s})}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡\\sqrt{s}+{cos}^{2}⁡\\sqrt{s}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{‖{T}^{′}(s)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}}\\right)}=4\\sqrt{s}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266137 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a0c45fb-1a1d-5177-bf4c-fd01be65faa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263096} {:answer/id #uuid "39c3dbdf-5f6f-5fe6-bac2-7cf9c7f67e86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263514} {:answer/id #uuid "4350ceb2-104a-5954-9cd1-0a02d74f4a77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263594} {:answer/id #uuid "9ccf270e-4167-5b66-a2b9-51b0179a8785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264341} {:answer/id #uuid "ad2ae9ed-c588-5454-885d-f17ba33f35b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264487}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263594} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ef9e59a-6517-5986-94c0-f586c58a7db0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "258f49b8-8aac-592e-a98b-1492e2d635c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-132122" :question/problem "Find the radius of the osculating circle at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ for the curve $r(t)=⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given only the curve $r(t)$, we will use the cross product formula to find the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),$ and $‖{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =⟨1,-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)‖ & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{″}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =⟨0,-{sec}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)$ and ${r}^{″}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\times {r}^{″}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,-2,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\times {r}^{″}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)‖ & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =\\frac{{‖{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\times {r}^{″}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\sqrt{2})^{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:answer/id #uuid "028b5d24-5343-5712-ab0f-d2940e077210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266165} {:answer/id #uuid "05babc80-2859-5f1a-8b0c-87dde6cecf89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266195} {:answer/id #uuid "1254fcec-98e0-5f67-a76b-6f8a8e44308a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266302} {:answer/id #uuid "1c7ced12-adf7-50f3-8fa2-2ec760ae813e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡t{cosh}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266386} {:answer/id #uuid "2296eb71-af04-5c41-943c-a5d4e6ebc126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266454} {:answer/id #uuid "238496c5-76bc-51bf-9369-36c9de851713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266471} {:answer/id #uuid "3703b92c-5129-5033-ab98-50cdcbc36343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡t\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2t\\sqrt{1+4{cosh}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266619} {:answer/id #uuid "3834cd2