ection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c7824f8f-c1b4-50c2-a8cc-85b1111053c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-142839" :question/problem "$\\frac{1-{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} & =\\frac{1-(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272381 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07c7e6e4-6e3b-56a4-91ed-0546fccc77de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269340} {:answer/id #uuid "0c71a31d-f139-51bd-b4cf-e748fbfc14d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269377} {:answer/id #uuid "324b8275-4933-57f5-92ff-07241bc0bbfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269725} {:answer/id #uuid "af9f4ce8-3a11-586d-a86e-d8ac271b215a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270832} {:answer/id #uuid "d1a55205-924e-560d-83d9-48c9876def6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271114}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269377} :answer-field/id #uuid "8488bcab-2186-5dfc-8fb3-c63329977205" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "144c40a8-184c-5b0c-9d8c-a01781e4fbf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-142842" :question/problem "$\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta }{1-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta }{1-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta }{1-(1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta }{1-1-{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =-\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =-\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta }{1-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272382 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53a1afef-ab20-5945-b76e-734ddce1d287" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+2{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270013} {:answer/id #uuid "640b4baa-bd5a-5438-8ead-3ad792f8ca79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270156} {:answer/id #uuid "9f59147e-3b45-5292-abf8-9bd74860dab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270682} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc3cba1-26e2-5c14-abf1-4ce11a76db7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2-{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271204} {:answer/id #uuid "f7d608dc-7308-59e2-ad6e-96afa80f19bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271442}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186270156} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb5b09ad-bc1f-512d-8096-60f9e316d665" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fc757669-b204-5044-83d4-679ef2bca4ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-142871" :question/problem "${cos}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\,({sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\,({sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x) & ={cos}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\,(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\\,{cos}^{2}⁡x=1-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identities, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡x}} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\,({sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x)=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272383 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03364fe5-c4cf-5047-9205-8b8f7865c01e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value 